WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.151
[musical swirl]

2
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.669
[electric chimes]

3
00:00:29.602 --> 00:00:31.522
[orchestra tuning]

4
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

5
00:00:42.545 --> 00:00:44.882
[soft music]

6
00:01:01.707 --> 00:01:03.418
[muffled sounds]

7
00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:07.595
[music swells]

8
00:01:09.765 --> 00:01:11.644
[birds chirping]

9
00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:20.203
[soft snoring]

10
00:01:20.495 --> 00:01:23.083
[distant Indian
war whoops and gunfire]

11
00:01:26.256 --> 00:01:27.926
[canon fire and yelling]

12
00:01:33.647 --> 00:01:34.982
[cannon fire booms]

13
00:01:36.904 --> 00:01:38.196
[cannon fire booms]

14
00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:43.123
[gasping]

15
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.762
[cacophony of
gunfire and yelling]

16
00:01:52.726 --> 00:01:54.062
[horse neighs]

17
00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.698
Where is the General?
Where is he?

18
00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:11.013
Where is Braddock?

19
00:02:13.475 --> 00:02:14.477
[gun cocks]

20
00:02:15.814 --> 00:02:16.649
What happened?

21
00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:17.943
We've been ambushed!

22
00:02:18.068 --> 00:02:18.737
From where?

23
00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:19.905
Over the hill!

24
00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:30.886
[panting]

25
00:02:31.303 --> 00:02:33.098
[sounds muffle.
gasping as ringing starts]

26
00:02:34.392 --> 00:02:36.104
[grunts. sounds returning]

27
00:02:41.615 --> 00:02:42.993
[dramatic music]

28
00:02:49.256 --> 00:02:50.801
[cannon fire booms]

29
00:02:51.134 --> 00:02:52.763
[dramatic music intensifies]

30
00:02:58.984 --> 00:03:00.027
[coughing]

31
00:03:03.617 --> 00:03:05.078
I wouldn't bother. Washington.

32
00:03:05.789 --> 00:03:06.999
The battle is lost.

33
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.251
Where is the General?

34
00:03:08.418 --> 00:03:09.588
Ordered a full retreat.

35
00:03:09.838 --> 00:03:11.800
That way lies nothing but death.

36
00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:12.803
And my men?

37
00:03:14.347 --> 00:03:15.098
You have no men.

38
00:03:15.223 --> 00:03:16.434
The Virginians.

39
00:03:17.187 --> 00:03:19.900
They were at
the front of the line.

40
00:03:21.737 --> 00:03:24.159
If you go that way.
you will die.

41
00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.747
You look like death already.

42
00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.000
Listen to me.

43
00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.007
You'll never find them.
and even if you did.

44
00:03:32.134 --> 00:03:33.511
you'd never make it back.

45
00:03:34.012 --> 00:03:35.263
[cannon fire booms]

46
00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:36.391
Washington.

47
00:03:37.269 --> 00:03:38.353
Washington!

48
00:03:39.231 --> 00:03:40.357
Come. my friend.

49
00:03:41.443 --> 00:03:43.572
What could be worth the risk?

50
00:03:43.697 --> 00:03:45.786
[dramatic stinger]

51
00:03:55.806 --> 00:03:57.434
[solemn music]

52
00:04:05.448 --> 00:04:07.077
[solemn music continues]

53
00:04:21.565 --> 00:04:22.818
-[Lawrence] Mary.

54
00:04:23.276 --> 00:04:24.196
I'm so sorry.

55
00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.494
This must be Jack.

56
00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.998
This is...our Jack

57
00:04:30.165 --> 00:04:31.459
[Mary whispers to baby]

58
00:04:32.462 --> 00:04:33.589
Where is he?

59
00:04:34.466 --> 00:04:35.342
He's there.

60
00:04:35.886 --> 00:04:37.848
He’s not spoken since...

61
00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:40.688
[Mary] since his father died.

62
00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.070
[solemn music continues]

63
00:04:54.798 --> 00:04:56.009
Hello. George.

64
00:05:05.152 --> 00:05:07.324
Do you remember me?

65
00:05:07.866 --> 00:05:09.537
I'm your half-brother.

66
00:05:09.995 --> 00:05:10.789
Lawrence.

67
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:13.877
You're an officer?

68
00:05:14.171 --> 00:05:15.380
I was. yes.

69
00:05:16.842 --> 00:05:19.181
Captain in his Majesty's Navy.

70
00:05:21.602 --> 00:05:23.396
I have something for you.

71
00:05:27.865 --> 00:05:29.577
It’s a surveyor’s compass.

72
00:05:29.702 --> 00:05:32.415
It measures distances
of land and sea.

73
00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:34.962
This was our father's.

74
00:05:35.714 --> 00:05:37.090
And now it's yours.

75
00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.927
Won’t you need it?

76
00:05:40.138 --> 00:05:43.395
Well. my next adventure is
here with you. George.

77
00:05:44.773 --> 00:05:48.280
I have been appointed Adjutant
General of the Virginia militia.

78
00:05:48.531 --> 00:05:50.911
So. you will command soldiers?

79
00:05:51.036 --> 00:05:52.873
I'm to organize militia.

80
00:05:54.668 --> 00:05:55.796
Volunteers. really.

81
00:05:57.716 --> 00:06:00.095
[wagon wheels rumbling]

82
00:06:02.685 --> 00:06:04.312
[mournful music plays]

83
00:06:16.962 --> 00:06:19.593
<i>[George] Do Washington</i>
<i>men die young?</i>

84
00:06:19.718 --> 00:06:20.678
<i>[Lawrence] What?</i>

85
00:06:20.971 --> 00:06:23.809
<i>[George] I heard them say</i>
<i>Washington men die young.</i>

86
00:06:23.976 --> 00:06:26.148
<i>That it's a curse to our name.</i>

87
00:06:27.399 --> 00:06:28.401
Is that true?

88
00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:32.745
Are you afraid to die?

89
00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.525
[George] Mother says I will
not be going back to school.

90
00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.903
[Lawrence] There's nothing
wrong with tenant farming.

91
00:06:50.028 --> 00:06:51.364
It's an honorable profession.

92
00:06:51.489 --> 00:06:53.201
[George] But that is not
what I want.

93
00:06:53.661 --> 00:06:55.330
[Lawrence] It's what
duty demands.

94
00:06:55.874 --> 00:06:58.295
Time and circumstance
have changed.

95
00:06:58.879 --> 00:07:01.134
William Fairfax
is attending school.

96
00:07:01.384 --> 00:07:02.260
Why can I not?

97
00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:05.267
The Fairfaxes
are of a superior class.

98
00:07:05.809 --> 00:07:08.857
With advantages we
will never possess. George.

99
00:07:09.066 --> 00:07:11.697
The world is
often an unfair place.

100
00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:17.040
And you must take what
it gives you and make it yours.

101
00:07:17.249 --> 00:07:18.376
Now come inside.

102
00:07:20.463 --> 00:07:22.425
[bright music plays]

103
00:07:24.431 --> 00:07:26.184
George. where are you going?

104
00:07:26.309 --> 00:07:27.352
To school!

105
00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:30.776
Stubborn child.

106
00:07:38.041 --> 00:07:39.167
[Lawrence] It's two miles.

107
00:07:39.878 --> 00:07:40.671
I know.

108
00:07:42.049 --> 00:07:43.844
They will not let you in.

109
00:07:43.969 --> 00:07:45.055
[George] They will.

110
00:07:48.854 --> 00:07:50.524
[axe thuds]

111
00:07:52.946 --> 00:07:54.449
Don't take it out on the tree.

112
00:07:54.742 --> 00:07:56.662
George. Stop. stop!

113
00:07:57.495 --> 00:07:58.415
[Mary sighs]

114
00:07:58.916 --> 00:08:01.296
They turned me away.
Because of you.

115
00:08:01.421 --> 00:08:03.050
And now I have nothing.

116
00:08:04.051 --> 00:08:04.928
Nothing?

117
00:08:05.053 --> 00:08:05.888
[scoffs]

118
00:08:06.181 --> 00:08:09.396
We have 250 acres.

119
00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:12.275
Ten slaves in bondage
to feed.

120
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.032
And one widow's purse.
near empty.

121
00:08:16.118 --> 00:08:18.205
You're the eldest son
in this house.

122
00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.000
and you have
a duty to it.

123
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.420
That is not what I want.
I want more than this.

124
00:08:22.588 --> 00:08:25.427
And I want a husband.
back from his fever.

125
00:08:25.636 --> 00:08:27.264
Providence denied me this.

126
00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:29.184
Then Providence is cruel!

127
00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:36.491
God raises
what is well grounded.

128
00:08:38.245 --> 00:08:41.041
You'll not abandon
what is yours. nor will I.

129
00:08:41.502 --> 00:08:42.921
You're my son.

130
00:08:43.046 --> 00:08:47.012
and a Washington.
and you'll behave like both.

131
00:08:49.016 --> 00:08:50.561
[Mary sighs deeply]

132
00:08:53.441 --> 00:08:54.317
[sighs]

133
00:08:57.324 --> 00:08:58.869
[door creaks open]

134
00:09:10.225 --> 00:09:12.062
[Lawrence breathes deeply]

135
00:09:21.248 --> 00:09:21.915
Here.

136
00:09:23.001 --> 00:09:25.839
Rules of Civility
and Decent Behavior.

137
00:09:25.964 --> 00:09:29.179
That will teach you
how to be a proper gentleman.

138
00:09:29.346 --> 00:09:33.313
Then Cato. Plutarch.
Essential readings.

139
00:09:34.525 --> 00:09:36.236
Seneca and Cincinnatus.

140
00:09:37.279 --> 00:09:41.454
If one desires to be great.
he must study those that were.

141
00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:44.628
It’s a lot of books. I know--

142
00:09:47.174 --> 00:09:49.972
I am sorry for
your misfortune. George.

143
00:09:51.139 --> 00:09:55.566
If no one else will
teach you. I'll teach you.

144
00:09:56.652 --> 00:09:58.446
But I could loan you these.

145
00:09:58.989 --> 00:10:00.659
one by one.

146
00:10:02.788 --> 00:10:04.374
if you do your chores.

147
00:10:06.296 --> 00:10:07.881
[bright music]

148
00:10:09.384 --> 00:10:11.974
[Lawrence] “Every public
action should” what?

149
00:10:12.099 --> 00:10:14.352
[George] “Show respect to
those who are present.”

150
00:10:14.477 --> 00:10:16.316
What do you
think respect means?

151
00:10:16.441 --> 00:10:20.115
<i>[George] To listen to or obey</i>
<i>the one you are respecting.</i>

152
00:10:20.783 --> 00:10:21.702
<i>[Lawrence] Perhaps.</i>

153
00:10:22.536 --> 00:10:24.750
<i>But obedience can be commanded.</i>

154
00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.212
<i>Respect must be earned.</i>

155
00:10:28.716 --> 00:10:31.053
<i>That is why I became a soldier.</i>

156
00:10:31.178 --> 00:10:33.391
<i>[bright music continues]</i>

157
00:10:34.602 --> 00:10:37.440
Aristocracy is a game. George.

158
00:10:37.566 --> 00:10:40.363
But. you could learn
to play it. I suppose.

159
00:10:40.488 --> 00:10:41.867
What piece are we?

160
00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.954
We are pawns. George.

161
00:10:46.627 --> 00:10:48.922
But even a pawn can take a king.

162
00:10:49.925 --> 00:10:50.968
Play again?

163
00:10:51.845 --> 00:10:52.721
Yeah.

164
00:10:53.431 --> 00:10:54.141
Up.

165
00:10:56.438 --> 00:10:57.898
<i>[Lawrence] Very nice. George.</i>

166
00:10:58.817 --> 00:11:01.029
[Lawrence] Remember. heels down.
chest up.

167
00:11:02.032 --> 00:11:04.202
I think it's
now time you ride alone.

168
00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:06.123
Wouldn't you agree?

169
00:11:06.248 --> 00:11:06.917
Yes.

170
00:11:07.042 --> 00:11:07.960
Very well.

171
00:11:08.086 --> 00:11:08.879
Go on then.

172
00:11:09.462 --> 00:11:11.258
[adventurous music]

173
00:11:11.719 --> 00:11:12.970
[Lawrence] Not too fast now.

174
00:11:14.181 --> 00:11:15.433
Steady.

175
00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:20.152
<i>[young George] “To obtain</i>
<i>the applause of</i>

176
00:11:20.277 --> 00:11:24.201
<i>deserving men</i>
<i>is a heartfelt satisfaction...”</i>

177
00:11:27.374 --> 00:11:29.294
[adventurous music swells]

178
00:11:29.419 --> 00:11:33.679
[George] “...to merit them
is my highest wish...”

179
00:11:44.827 --> 00:11:46.705
[indistinct chatter]

180
00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.462
<i>[Col. Gooch] So. here he is.</i>

181
00:11:50.588 --> 00:11:53.050
<i>The boy who</i>
<i>writes all the letters...</i>

182
00:11:53.176 --> 00:11:55.222
petitioning for a
‘royal’ commission?

183
00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:56.014
Yes. sir.

184
00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.436
I dream of
becoming a British officer.

185
00:11:58.604 --> 00:12:01.358
Ensign or lieutenant.
as his Majesty sees fit.

186
00:12:02.235 --> 00:12:04.698
I believe my brother
communicated this on my behalf.

187
00:12:05.117 --> 00:12:06.409
Lawrence Washington.

188
00:12:06.537 --> 00:12:07.871
He served under the--

189
00:12:07.996 --> 00:12:10.628
If I were to allow it...
the purchase price

190
00:12:10.753 --> 00:12:13.842
for an ensigncy in the
Coldstreams is £700.

191
00:12:13.967 --> 00:12:15.303
Do you possess that. sir?

192
00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:16.682
No. sir. I do not.

193
00:12:16.807 --> 00:12:18.769
Then why not
seek to join the militia?

194
00:12:18.894 --> 00:12:21.525
Well. I wish to serve
the Crown as an actual officer.

195
00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.112
Then how much
land do you possess?

196
00:12:24.279 --> 00:12:26.952
I am a custodian. um.
under my brother's estate

197
00:12:27.077 --> 00:12:27.995
at Mount Vernon.

198
00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.122
Tenant farmer.

199
00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:31.001
Education?

200
00:12:31.168 --> 00:12:34.675
I received no formal schooling
after my father died. sir.

201
00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.764
But I recently obtained
my surveyor's license.

202
00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:38.559
To be a British officer.

203
00:12:38.809 --> 00:12:40.938
you must first be a gentleman.

204
00:12:41.229 --> 00:12:43.861
If I may. sir. how is it that my
brother qualified yet I do not?

205
00:12:43.986 --> 00:12:45.238
He owns Mount Vernon.

206
00:12:45.363 --> 00:12:47.910
He was properly
educated in England.

207
00:12:48.035 --> 00:12:49.663
And what's more.
he's married to a Fairfax.

208
00:12:49.788 --> 00:12:52.210
Yes. and he has
been a great mentor to me.

209
00:12:52.335 --> 00:12:54.507
I-I've studied
to become a gentleman.

210
00:12:54.632 --> 00:12:56.595
I've even compiled
all I've learned.

211
00:12:56.762 --> 00:12:59.432
Goodness. man.
how much do you write?

212
00:12:59.725 --> 00:13:01.103
Well. I've compiled
it from other books.

213
00:13:01.228 --> 00:13:02.981
It's called Rules of
Civility and Decent Behaviour.

214
00:13:03.106 --> 00:13:05.028
Which is to say
you plagiarised it.

215
00:13:05.153 --> 00:13:05.946
No. No. no--

216
00:13:06.657 --> 00:13:07.866
Well. yes. but. err...

217
00:13:08.827 --> 00:13:12.042
Imitation of great men
does not make you one.

218
00:13:16.383 --> 00:13:17.260
I... I ask again. sir.

219
00:13:17.385 --> 00:13:19.181
How may I become a
British officer of the Crown?

220
00:13:19.306 --> 00:13:20.643
-You cannot--
-There must be a path.

221
00:13:20.768 --> 00:13:23.356
There is not for you.

222
00:13:24.733 --> 00:13:27.906
And please.
stop writing me letters.

223
00:13:34.795 --> 00:13:35.463
Go!

224
00:13:36.214 --> 00:13:37.510
[dramatic music]

225
00:14:07.152 --> 00:14:08.236
[George] Hello. Jack.

226
00:14:10.075 --> 00:14:11.326
Good to see you.

227
00:14:12.871 --> 00:14:14.499
Are you an officer now?

228
00:14:15.293 --> 00:14:15.961
Not yet.

229
00:14:17.047 --> 00:14:17.798
But someday.

230
00:14:18.509 --> 00:14:19.467
[Mary] Or never.

231
00:14:21.054 --> 00:14:22.975
If God hears my prayers.

232
00:14:36.795 --> 00:14:38.338
“Be not tedious in discourse.”

233
00:14:38.757 --> 00:14:40.008
[exhales]

234
00:14:40.135 --> 00:14:41.512
Especially tonight.

235
00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.267
[distant footfalls]

236
00:14:47.608 --> 00:14:49.277
Where are you off to?

237
00:14:51.198 --> 00:14:52.325
To see Lawrence.

238
00:14:52.951 --> 00:14:57.044
At Belvoir? You're not invited.
How do you expect to get in?

239
00:14:57.169 --> 00:14:59.172
Is it a sin to seek advancement?

240
00:14:59.297 --> 00:15:00.300
It is to them.

241
00:15:02.054 --> 00:15:03.516
You're just a pawn to them.

242
00:15:06.186 --> 00:15:09.067
Well. even a pawn
can take a king.

243
00:15:13.033 --> 00:15:14.578
[noble fanfare]

244
00:15:14.953 --> 00:15:16.414
[classical music plays]

245
00:15:26.393 --> 00:15:27.395
[Steward] Invitation. sir.

246
00:15:27.521 --> 00:15:30.861
I am Mr. Washington. uh.
George Washington.

247
00:15:31.737 --> 00:15:33.073
Half-brother to Lawrence.

248
00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:36.121
who is married to Anne.
formerly Fairfax.

249
00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.463
Thank you for the genealogy.
Now. your invitation. sir?

250
00:15:40.589 --> 00:15:41.256
Ah.

251
00:15:42.635 --> 00:15:44.012
Um...I don't have it.

252
00:15:45.348 --> 00:15:47.019
The guests for this party
have been chosen

253
00:15:47.144 --> 00:15:50.358
with great specificity.
so I suggest you find it.

254
00:15:50.483 --> 00:15:51.569
Mr. Washington.

255
00:15:52.988 --> 00:15:53.657
Sir.

256
00:15:55.242 --> 00:15:56.244
Ah...

257
00:15:56.704 --> 00:15:57.873
-Good evening.
-Thank you.

258
00:16:01.839 --> 00:16:04.595
[curious music]

259
00:16:11.942 --> 00:16:13.906
[laughter]

260
00:16:33.652 --> 00:16:34.487
Good evening.

261
00:16:34.613 --> 00:16:35.322
-Good evening.
-Evening. sir.

262
00:16:35.448 --> 00:16:36.867
We need more ice.

263
00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.582
Uh. can I. can I carry
that upstairs?

264
00:16:39.707 --> 00:16:40.876
Uh. no need. sir.

265
00:16:44.717 --> 00:16:46.595
How-how do I get in
the house?

266
00:16:48.557 --> 00:16:50.563
[string music plays]

267
00:17:08.974 --> 00:17:10.350
[woman] You don't
belong here.

268
00:17:13.106 --> 00:17:15.027
Clever entrance. though.

269
00:17:15.988 --> 00:17:18.241
Most guests just
enter through the front door.

270
00:17:18.366 --> 00:17:20.873
My brother spoke to
me of this gathering. He is--

271
00:17:20.998 --> 00:17:22.626
Married to Ann Fairfax.

272
00:17:23.251 --> 00:17:24.379
Yes. I know.

273
00:17:25.549 --> 00:17:27.845
You. on the
other hand. are not.

274
00:17:28.303 --> 00:17:29.848
A child of one of Virginia's

275
00:17:29.973 --> 00:17:32.437
largest fortunes and
family estates?

276
00:17:32.563 --> 00:17:34.149
You're right. I'm not.

277
00:17:34.858 --> 00:17:36.862
And you were right. I'm rich.

278
00:17:37.573 --> 00:17:38.574
But...

279
00:17:38.741 --> 00:17:40.410
I also don't feel
like I belong.

280
00:17:40.538 --> 00:17:43.375
Well. that's like saying a rose
doesn't belong in a garden.

281
00:17:46.256 --> 00:17:48.135
I'll take that compliment.

282
00:17:48.385 --> 00:17:50.891
I'd be happy
if there were more.

283
00:17:52.603 --> 00:17:56.401
Here's the problem with
trying to sneak into a party.

284
00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.992
You. sir. stand out in a crowd.

285
00:18:02.247 --> 00:18:03.624
Then dance with me.

286
00:18:03.832 --> 00:18:06.213
I only dance
with invited guests.

287
00:18:06.672 --> 00:18:09.928
Well. perhaps you should make
room for someone truly worthy.

288
00:18:10.053 --> 00:18:13.143
Because. I don’t see anyone
like that here.

289
00:18:14.062 --> 00:18:17.402
Mr. Washington. aren't you bold?

290
00:18:20.448 --> 00:18:21.451
Well. I'm off.

291
00:18:21.577 --> 00:18:22.287
To where?

292
00:18:24.124 --> 00:18:26.294
To fulfill my solemn duty.

293
00:18:28.757 --> 00:18:29.760
Charm.

294
00:18:34.186 --> 00:18:36.607
<i>[Lawrence] Gently does it.</i>
<i>George.</i>

295
00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.780
<i>Best to proceed with caution.</i>

296
00:18:40.155 --> 00:18:42.159
<i>It would profit Sally's</i>
<i>family greatly</i>

297
00:18:42.285 --> 00:18:44.707
<i>if she were to</i>
<i>marry a Fairfax.</i>

298
00:18:44.832 --> 00:18:46.043
Like you did?

299
00:18:46.877 --> 00:18:48.005
[Lawrence chuckles]

300
00:18:48.756 --> 00:18:49.466
Yes.

301
00:18:50.761 --> 00:18:54.351
And until I did. I held all my
hopes very loosely.

302
00:18:55.771 --> 00:18:57.941
The odds were against me.

303
00:19:00.487 --> 00:19:03.577
Well. the odds
have always been against us.

304
00:19:03.702 --> 00:19:04.622
Wish me luck.

305
00:19:06.166 --> 00:19:06.875
Good luck.

306
00:19:09.882 --> 00:19:11.468
[indistinct conversation]

307
00:19:13.388 --> 00:19:16.353
William. Thank you for
having me in your home.

308
00:19:16.478 --> 00:19:18.315
George. what a surprise.

309
00:19:19.067 --> 00:19:21.697
I didn't expect to
see you in a place like this.

310
00:19:21.822 --> 00:19:23.283
How ever did you get in?

311
00:19:23.408 --> 00:19:26.582
I was enticed by the
promise of beautiful women.

312
00:19:26.707 --> 00:19:28.586
Well. we'd
hate to disappoint you.

313
00:19:28.711 --> 00:19:29.755
You haven't.

314
00:19:30.758 --> 00:19:32.217
Meet Thomas Gage.

315
00:19:32.427 --> 00:19:35.851
Newly minted Major.
recently arrived from London

316
00:19:35.976 --> 00:19:37.227
by order of the Crown.

317
00:19:38.271 --> 00:19:38.939
Pleasure.

318
00:19:39.066 --> 00:19:39.775
Pleasure is mine.

319
00:19:40.275 --> 00:19:42.154
I. too. one day
hope to serve His Majesty.

320
00:19:42.405 --> 00:19:45.160
Tell me. Washington.
what is your opinion

321
00:19:45.285 --> 00:19:48.083
of the French
building forts on our land?

322
00:19:48.208 --> 00:19:50.839
Well. I think the Ohio
is a frontier.

323
00:19:50.964 --> 00:19:52.551
It belongs to the one
who tames it.

324
00:19:52.676 --> 00:19:53.802
-[William] Ah.
-Well said.

325
00:19:54.555 --> 00:19:59.021
But in reality. it belongs to
the one who buys it.

326
00:19:59.648 --> 00:20:01.401
That is the way
of things. is it not?

327
00:20:01.527 --> 00:20:02.863
[a minuet begins to play]

328
00:20:03.238 --> 00:20:07.204
Ah. a minuet.
I love a minuet.

329
00:20:07.998 --> 00:20:11.880
I believe I have the first
dance. if you'll excuse us.

330
00:20:17.057 --> 00:20:19.187
Pleasure to meet you.
I hope we meet again.

331
00:20:19.312 --> 00:20:20.188
Pleasure.

332
00:20:24.532 --> 00:20:26.034
-Where are you off to?
-Sally.

333
00:20:26.284 --> 00:20:27.663
My solemn duty.

334
00:20:37.516 --> 00:20:38.934
[deep sigh]

335
00:20:44.487 --> 00:20:45.447
Ah!

336
00:20:47.409 --> 00:20:49.372
Lord Fairfax.
Begging your pardon.

337
00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:52.671
I've dreamed of
seeing your library.

338
00:20:54.592 --> 00:20:56.469
These are my true tenants.

339
00:20:58.599 --> 00:20:59.643
Who are you?

340
00:20:59.768 --> 00:21:02.480
George Washington. sir.
Brother to Lawrence.

341
00:21:02.608 --> 00:21:04.192
I didn't know he'd invited you.

342
00:21:04.319 --> 00:21:05.989
Neither did he.
if you must know.

343
00:21:06.114 --> 00:21:09.955
Ah! So. I've caught
you slipping in.

344
00:21:10.205 --> 00:21:11.374
And you...

345
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.087
caught me slipping out. Come.

346
00:21:15.423 --> 00:21:16.885
I can't take much
of these soirées.

347
00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.639
So. I hide.

348
00:21:19.642 --> 00:21:22.981
Until my wife finds me
and rousts me back out.

349
00:21:24.484 --> 00:21:27.991
"When vice prevails. and
impious men bear sway.

350
00:21:28.116 --> 00:21:30.998
the post of
honor is a private station."

351
00:21:31.164 --> 00:21:32.124
Cato.

352
00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:33.711
You've seen the play?

353
00:21:33.836 --> 00:21:36.216
No. but I've read it
50 times over.

354
00:21:36.341 --> 00:21:38.596
"Tis not in mortals
to command success.

355
00:21:39.179 --> 00:21:41.059
But we'll do more.
We'll deserve it."

356
00:21:41.268 --> 00:21:42.646
Well said. [chuckles]

357
00:21:43.396 --> 00:21:45.901
Do you happen to
have Pope's Essay on Man?

358
00:21:46.028 --> 00:21:47.948
Would it be imposing if I
asked to borrow it?

359
00:21:48.741 --> 00:21:50.953
I obtained a letter of
introduction from your cousin.

360
00:21:51.997 --> 00:21:54.126
An eccentric fellow. isn't he?

361
00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:55.588
Indeed he is.

362
00:21:56.256 --> 00:21:58.761
He lent me a book on surveying
from his library.

363
00:21:58.886 --> 00:22:00.681
Not nearly as grand as yours.

364
00:22:00.806 --> 00:22:03.020
I put it to good use
and obtained my license.

365
00:22:03.145 --> 00:22:05.148
I know you own
five million acres now.

366
00:22:05.774 --> 00:22:07.821
The only thing
a landowner ever desires...

367
00:22:09.658 --> 00:22:11.369
is the plot next to his.

368
00:22:13.123 --> 00:22:13.832
Yes. I do.

369
00:22:15.168 --> 00:22:17.841
I also know a
great amount of that land

370
00:22:17.966 --> 00:22:21.431
is in the Ohio Valley
and has not been charted.

371
00:22:21.765 --> 00:22:25.188
I sense a looming storm
over the Ohio Territory.

372
00:22:26.817 --> 00:22:27.945
Inevitable. I'm afraid.

373
00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.740
I could go there.

374
00:22:29.865 --> 00:22:31.952
Survey it and map it for you.

375
00:22:32.285 --> 00:22:33.581
A land that isn't
properly measured

376
00:22:33.706 --> 00:22:34.917
cannot be properly valued.

377
00:22:35.042 --> 00:22:36.211
or protected.

378
00:22:36.336 --> 00:22:38.340
Much of that
territory is unexplored.

379
00:22:38.465 --> 00:22:40.553
Many have traveled there.
never to be seen again.

380
00:22:40.678 --> 00:22:41.346
Yes.

381
00:22:42.515 --> 00:22:44.812
But no man who
lived a life of ease

382
00:22:44.937 --> 00:22:47.691
ever left a name
worth remembering. sir.

383
00:22:47.818 --> 00:22:49.487
I'll take the risk upon myself.

384
00:22:49.613 --> 00:22:50.488
I'll make it to the furthest

385
00:22:50.614 --> 00:22:52.911
reaches of your
plot and report back.

386
00:22:53.036 --> 00:22:55.082
And I'll put my name
to that promise.

387
00:22:55.207 --> 00:22:57.419
Is this man bothering you. sir?

388
00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:02.638
Hardly.

389
00:23:03.599 --> 00:23:05.811
I accept your proposal. George.

390
00:23:06.188 --> 00:23:07.272
Thank you. sir.

391
00:23:08.358 --> 00:23:10.362
[spirited. upbeat music]

392
00:23:14.622 --> 00:23:16.625
Enjoy the party. Washington.

393
00:23:19.507 --> 00:23:21.594
[indistinct chatter]

394
00:23:25.475 --> 00:23:26.895
[man] Get out of the way.

395
00:23:33.951 --> 00:23:35.162
Christopher Gist.

396
00:23:37.082 --> 00:23:38.001
George?

397
00:23:38.961 --> 00:23:39.630
George.

398
00:23:43.637 --> 00:23:44.471
Good to see you.

399
00:23:44.598 --> 00:23:45.724
It's good to see you.

400
00:23:46.268 --> 00:23:49.775
George. these are the brothers
Frisk. Henry. the oldest.

401
00:23:50.067 --> 00:23:52.070
And his baby brother. David.

402
00:23:52.404 --> 00:23:54.241
[Christopher] My two
most loyal friends.

403
00:23:55.243 --> 00:23:55.911
Do not trust them.

404
00:23:56.036 --> 00:23:57.247
[laughs]

405
00:23:57.581 --> 00:23:59.209
That's a nice coat
you got there.

406
00:23:59.376 --> 00:24:00.879
Careful! He's a thief!

407
00:24:01.004 --> 00:24:01.757
Shut your--

408
00:24:01.882 --> 00:24:03.135
Leave him alone!

409
00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:07.059
Where are you
coming from. all...

410
00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:08.854
fresh and plucked?

411
00:24:10.899 --> 00:24:11.569
Belvoir.

412
00:24:11.944 --> 00:24:13.697
[mockingly] Ooh!

413
00:24:14.617 --> 00:24:18.206
That mean you too fancy to. uh.
place a little wager?

414
00:24:22.631 --> 00:24:23.926
How bout you place one for me?

415
00:24:24.051 --> 00:24:24.887
[laughs]

416
00:24:25.012 --> 00:24:26.890
Oh. I like him.

417
00:24:27.015 --> 00:24:28.393
What are you doing here?

418
00:24:28.519 --> 00:24:29.938
I have a job for us.

419
00:24:30.230 --> 00:24:31.859
I'm too drunk for work.

420
00:24:32.025 --> 00:24:34.362
Ambition waits for no man.

421
00:24:34.572 --> 00:24:35.365
What is it?

422
00:24:35.574 --> 00:24:37.745
Surveying the Ohio territory.

423
00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:39.750
I need someone who can
keep me alive.

424
00:24:40.709 --> 00:24:41.378
For who?

425
00:24:41.795 --> 00:24:42.713
Lord Fairfax.

426
00:24:44.968 --> 00:24:46.053
What part?

427
00:24:46.178 --> 00:24:47.389
Most all of it.

428
00:24:47.723 --> 00:24:48.976
He pays by the acre.

429
00:24:49.895 --> 00:24:50.896
[Henry laughs]

430
00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:55.614
Well...

431
00:24:56.617 --> 00:24:57.910
let's get it done.

432
00:24:58.120 --> 00:24:59.079
[laughs]

433
00:24:59.873 --> 00:25:00.749
To Virginia!

434
00:25:01.376 --> 00:25:02.252
To Virginia!

435
00:25:03.839 --> 00:25:05.926
[spirited. upbeat
music continues]

436
00:25:06.051 --> 00:25:08.431
That is the last time.
Henry!

437
00:25:08.682 --> 00:25:09.349
David!

438
00:25:09.683 --> 00:25:10.728
[incoherent yelling]

439
00:25:10.853 --> 00:25:12.480
She's your mother. too!

440
00:25:13.108 --> 00:25:14.778
Yeah. we don't
know that for sure.

441
00:25:15.028 --> 00:25:15.946
[men yelling fades out]

442
00:25:17.575 --> 00:25:20.664
[adventurous music]

443
00:25:22.543 --> 00:25:24.004
[George] It's beautiful.
isn't it?

444
00:25:24.672 --> 00:25:25.340
Yeah.

445
00:25:28.681 --> 00:25:30.601
But it don't belong to you.

446
00:25:31.226 --> 00:25:35.152
Well. if we go far enough.
it doesn't belong to anyone.

447
00:25:40.495 --> 00:25:41.749
<i>[George] Dear madam.</i>

448
00:25:42.249 --> 00:25:45.839
<i>Gazing at the new world.</i>
<i>I now write to express my joy.</i>

449
00:25:46.381 --> 00:25:47.342
<i>I was honored with</i>
<i>your short</i>

450
00:25:47.551 --> 00:25:51.183
<i>but very agreeable favor</i>
<i>of our first acquaintance.</i>

451
00:25:52.310 --> 00:25:53.271
In this case.

452
00:25:53.396 --> 00:25:56.193
<i>the one who is too sensible of</i>
<i>her charms to deny the power.</i>

453
00:25:56.318 --> 00:25:58.949
<i>whose influence I feel</i>
<i>and must ever submit to.</i>

454
00:25:59.407 --> 00:26:01.997
<i>I am aware of</i>
<i>how impossible this is. But...</i>

455
00:26:02.330 --> 00:26:03.709
<i>if you will allow me</i>
<i>to prove myself.</i>

456
00:26:03.876 --> 00:26:06.171
<i>I pledge to rule out</i>
<i>all disappointment.</i>

457
00:26:10.973 --> 00:26:13.729
<i>I wish I could be with you.</i>
<i>Or rather. you here with me.</i>

458
00:26:14.062 --> 00:26:17.653
<i>So you could witness the</i>
<i>beauty of this land.</i>

459
00:26:19.072 --> 00:26:20.408
Let's see who this is.

460
00:26:20.534 --> 00:26:22.120
Pass it-- pass it back.
Pass it back.

461
00:26:22.245 --> 00:26:23.999
Miss Sally Cary?

462
00:26:27.130 --> 00:26:30.178
You might as well petition the
Queen of England. George.

463
00:26:30.303 --> 00:26:32.099
She's above your station.

464
00:26:32.683 --> 00:26:33.561
Permanently.

465
00:26:35.606 --> 00:26:38.320
Fight battles you can win.
George.

466
00:26:39.990 --> 00:26:41.449
Nice signature. though.

467
00:26:42.745 --> 00:26:45.668
“I am your humble
devoted servant”.

468
00:26:48.005 --> 00:26:49.132
[rushing water]

469
00:26:57.525 --> 00:26:58.819
[horse neighing]

470
00:27:00.573 --> 00:27:02.367
[Christopher] We're not
going to make it back

471
00:27:02.576 --> 00:27:04.079
before winter sets in.

472
00:27:04.622 --> 00:27:06.374
[George] The horses
have done all they can.

473
00:27:07.210 --> 00:27:08.589
We must leave them.

474
00:27:09.339 --> 00:27:10.718
There’s a village.

475
00:27:10.884 --> 00:27:13.682
about a half a day’s
journey from here.

476
00:27:14.432 --> 00:27:15.644
We could shelter.

477
00:27:16.186 --> 00:27:16.939
Ride out the cold.

478
00:27:17.064 --> 00:27:18.692
No. no. that's too long a time.

479
00:27:18.817 --> 00:27:21.363
[shivering] I suppose you'd
rather freeze to death.

480
00:27:22.783 --> 00:27:24.119
We have to return.

481
00:27:24.662 --> 00:27:25.748
So you can see your
woman?

482
00:27:25.998 --> 00:27:27.375
So we can get paid.

483
00:27:28.378 --> 00:27:31.885
It’s unbecoming of a gentleman
to lie to himself.

484
00:27:33.136 --> 00:27:34.097
[whistles]

485
00:27:37.479 --> 00:27:39.399
[ominous music]

486
00:27:44.535 --> 00:27:46.664
[Christopher speaks Seneca]

487
00:27:52.926 --> 00:27:54.638
[speaking Seneca]

488
00:27:58.731 --> 00:28:01.151
He's not too
fond of your compass.

489
00:28:02.821 --> 00:28:04.074
Offer them the horses.

490
00:28:04.199 --> 00:28:04.992
George?

491
00:28:05.118 --> 00:28:06.747
They’re no longer
of use to us...

492
00:28:06.872 --> 00:28:09.417
but they could still be
saved to serve them.

493
00:28:09.543 --> 00:28:11.171
You offer dying horses?

494
00:28:13.258 --> 00:28:15.973
For the land
given to me by my father?

495
00:28:17.475 --> 00:28:18.812
To him by his father?

496
00:28:18.937 --> 00:28:20.315
Hey... hey.

497
00:28:22.152 --> 00:28:25.826
You have no right to take
what we possess for generations.

498
00:28:25.951 --> 00:28:28.456
We are not here
to claim this land.

499
00:28:31.253 --> 00:28:32.840
We are surveyors only.

500
00:28:55.594 --> 00:28:57.973
I know what
you want. Englishman.

501
00:28:59.059 --> 00:29:00.437
And I offer something
more.

502
00:29:04.277 --> 00:29:05.989
Something for your king.

503
00:29:12.545 --> 00:29:14.297
[dramatic music]

504
00:29:25.068 --> 00:29:26.321
Whose fort is that?

505
00:29:28.283 --> 00:29:29.411
The French.

506
00:29:33.921 --> 00:29:35.799
[dramatic music continues]

507
00:29:38.681 --> 00:29:39.973
[Christopher] Are you
sure

508
00:29:40.098 --> 00:29:41.937
this is the fastest way home?

509
00:29:42.771 --> 00:29:44.107
[George] Saves us two days.

510
00:29:44.232 --> 00:29:45.611
[Christopher] If we fall off
this raft.

511
00:29:45.736 --> 00:29:47.030
we'll freeze to death.

512
00:29:47.155 --> 00:29:48.742
No. no. We have to get
this information back.

513
00:29:49.910 --> 00:29:50.579
[grunts]

514
00:29:50.704 --> 00:29:52.791
You're full of
surprises. you know.

515
00:29:52.916 --> 00:29:54.211
Speaking their tongue?

516
00:29:54.920 --> 00:29:56.632
Well...”know thy enemy.”

517
00:29:57.009 --> 00:29:58.385
Are they the enemy?

518
00:29:58.637 --> 00:29:59.722
They let us go.

519
00:30:00.055 --> 00:30:02.185
Only because they hate
the French more than--

520
00:30:02.310 --> 00:30:04.022
More than they hate us.

521
00:30:07.445 --> 00:30:08.113
George.

522
00:30:08.238 --> 00:30:09.366
George. look!

523
00:30:09.617 --> 00:30:10.619
Look. look.

524
00:30:17.883 --> 00:30:18.886
Get to the shore!

525
00:30:19.011 --> 00:30:20.262
[both grunt with effort]

526
00:30:21.098 --> 00:30:21.807
Push!

527
00:30:22.017 --> 00:30:22.726
I'm trying.

528
00:30:22.851 --> 00:30:23.561
Get to the shore!

529
00:30:23.729 --> 00:30:25.440
The current is too strong.

530
00:30:27.570 --> 00:30:28.361
No.

531
00:30:30.701 --> 00:30:31.702
Christopher...

532
00:30:31.910 --> 00:30:32.871
Hold on. hold on.

533
00:30:32.996 --> 00:30:34.374
[both yell]

534
00:30:35.794 --> 00:30:37.089
[music intensifies]

535
00:30:38.006 --> 00:30:39.176
[gasps]

536
00:30:48.068 --> 00:30:49.071
[George] Swim!

537
00:30:50.280 --> 00:30:51.158
[Christopher] The maps!

538
00:30:51.449 --> 00:30:52.745
[George] Christopher!

539
00:30:52.953 --> 00:30:55.918
[dramatic music]

540
00:30:59.925 --> 00:31:01.053
Did you get the maps?

541
00:31:02.472 --> 00:31:03.976
[grunts]

542
00:31:16.208 --> 00:31:17.503
[grunts]

543
00:31:17.628 --> 00:31:18.671
[both shivering]

544
00:31:19.089 --> 00:31:21.969
George. you think
you could swim across?

545
00:31:23.932 --> 00:31:25.183
[grunts]

546
00:31:30.443 --> 00:31:32.157
Stay awake. George.

547
00:31:37.459 --> 00:31:39.004
Save your strength.

548
00:31:58.250 --> 00:31:59.127
Christopher.

549
00:32:01.339 --> 00:32:02.593
Christopher. wake up.

550
00:32:02.718 --> 00:32:03.385
Wake up!

551
00:32:04.471 --> 00:32:05.347
Christopher!

552
00:32:07.394 --> 00:32:09.064
[Christopher breathes
raggedly]

553
00:32:11.443 --> 00:32:13.155
You believe in miracles?

554
00:32:19.960 --> 00:32:20.671
Get up.

555
00:32:20.796 --> 00:32:22.089
How did it freeze?

556
00:32:25.095 --> 00:32:26.932
Do we risk it?

557
00:32:36.201 --> 00:32:37.788
[gasps]

558
00:32:46.514 --> 00:32:47.975
[Lawrence coughs]

559
00:32:53.151 --> 00:32:54.655
You can confirm this?

560
00:32:55.699 --> 00:32:56.366
Yes.

561
00:32:56.950 --> 00:32:58.787
So can Christopher Gist.

562
00:32:59.122 --> 00:33:00.123
[coughs]

563
00:33:01.209 --> 00:33:05.008
If you have these delivered to
Governor Dinwiddie. he can...

564
00:33:08.181 --> 00:33:09.309
Consumption.

565
00:33:10.561 --> 00:33:11.271
They say.

566
00:33:11.689 --> 00:33:12.858
[Lawrence coughs]

567
00:33:17.660 --> 00:33:19.412
All men die. George.

568
00:33:20.413 --> 00:33:22.419
I can't go to the governor
in my state.

569
00:33:23.587 --> 00:33:24.798
[coughs]

570
00:33:25.508 --> 00:33:27.888
You wish to
advance your station?

571
00:33:29.266 --> 00:33:31.562
My condition
may be your answer.

572
00:33:31.687 --> 00:33:33.566
[coughs]

573
00:33:39.034 --> 00:33:40.579
[coughs]

574
00:33:41.624 --> 00:33:43.210
[coughs]

575
00:33:47.134 --> 00:33:48.220
[church bells toll]

576
00:33:48.386 --> 00:33:49.682
[indistinct chatter]

577
00:33:55.108 --> 00:33:57.320
You saw these
things with your own eyes.

578
00:33:57.447 --> 00:33:58.574
Yes. Your Excellency.

579
00:33:58.782 --> 00:34:00.913
On land owned
rightly and duly by us --

580
00:34:01.038 --> 00:34:02.750
Well. the-- the Fairfaxes.

581
00:34:02.875 --> 00:34:05.671
I also own a significant
share of land there.

582
00:34:05.798 --> 00:34:07.635
This French encroachment
cannot stand.

583
00:34:07.760 --> 00:34:09.262
They must be told
to abandon it.

584
00:34:09.387 --> 00:34:11.934
By whom. sir? We don't
even know where they are.

585
00:34:12.059 --> 00:34:13.395
I do. sir.

586
00:34:13.854 --> 00:34:15.818
I could lead this expedition.

587
00:34:15.943 --> 00:34:18.155
To deliver your demands
to the French.

588
00:34:18.280 --> 00:34:20.158
I know the land. sir.
better than anyone.

589
00:34:20.283 --> 00:34:21.244
You?

590
00:34:21.411 --> 00:34:23.498
In the 15 years since the
Crown sent me to serve.

591
00:34:23.624 --> 00:34:26.547
I've yet to have a good
experience with a...colonist.

592
00:34:26.672 --> 00:34:28.216
Well. I look forward
to changing your opinion.

593
00:34:28.341 --> 00:34:30.012
If there used to be a
colonial expedition.

594
00:34:30.137 --> 00:34:31.932
it would be led
by your own brother.

595
00:34:32.057 --> 00:34:33.519
He commands the militia.

596
00:34:33.644 --> 00:34:35.105
Lawrences health fails him. sir.

597
00:34:35.230 --> 00:34:38.153
And he is no longer able to
fulfill the duties of his post.

598
00:34:38.445 --> 00:34:39.447
Here.

599
00:34:40.198 --> 00:34:42.788
He recommends me
as his replacement.

600
00:34:46.504 --> 00:34:48.131
So you have ambition?

601
00:34:48.256 --> 00:34:49.760
Yes. sir. I do.

602
00:34:50.385 --> 00:34:52.808
I see you met the savage
we call the Half-King.

603
00:34:52.933 --> 00:34:54.311
I have met the man.

604
00:34:54.436 --> 00:34:56.565
He led me to this information.
but...

605
00:34:56.690 --> 00:34:59.321
whether he can be trusted...
I’m not certain.

606
00:34:59.446 --> 00:35:01.742
I should be
alarmed if you were.

607
00:35:03.286 --> 00:35:05.457
Go and parley with
this Half-King.

608
00:35:05.583 --> 00:35:07.127
learn all you can from him.

609
00:35:07.252 --> 00:35:08.839
Then take your men
to Fort LeBoeuf.

610
00:35:08.964 --> 00:35:10.676
demand the French leave.

611
00:35:11.595 --> 00:35:14.685
My...my...my men. sir?

612
00:35:14.810 --> 00:35:18.316
Yes. Recruit 150
of your fellow Virginians.

613
00:35:18.651 --> 00:35:21.532
Lead them and
deliver this message.

614
00:35:22.449 --> 00:35:24.077
Which says what. sir?

615
00:35:24.202 --> 00:35:26.208
That they leave immediately.

616
00:35:26.792 --> 00:35:28.128
And if the French refuse?

617
00:35:28.253 --> 00:35:29.757
Do not permit them to refuse.

618
00:35:29.882 --> 00:35:31.176
So. then I am to fight?

619
00:35:31.301 --> 00:35:34.181
You are to deliver a message
and await further orders.

620
00:35:34.307 --> 00:35:35.475
[Gage] Your Excellency.
if I may.

621
00:35:35.601 --> 00:35:36.979
Will he not need the assistance

622
00:35:37.104 --> 00:35:38.941
of professional soldiers
of the Crown?

623
00:35:39.317 --> 00:35:43.534
No. militia will do. Especially
under one of such ambition.

624
00:35:44.578 --> 00:35:47.918
You shall receive the rank of
Major in the Virginia militia.

625
00:35:48.043 --> 00:35:50.130
which is not a
royal commission. understood?

626
00:35:50.255 --> 00:35:51.216
Mmm.

627
00:35:52.342 --> 00:35:56.644
There is an interpreter here.
Van Braam. Dutchman. Take him.

628
00:35:57.771 --> 00:36:00.358
Will my men and
I receive equal pay. sir?

629
00:36:00.609 --> 00:36:01.278
To whom?

630
00:36:02.404 --> 00:36:04.660
British officers of the Crown.

631
00:36:04.785 --> 00:36:06.997
Mr. Washington. you've just
advanced from farmer

632
00:36:07.122 --> 00:36:08.751
to Major in a
matter of seconds.

633
00:36:08.876 --> 00:36:11.507
What you ask for is
offensive to me.

634
00:36:11.632 --> 00:36:14.011
Then I will
volunteer my service.

635
00:36:14.429 --> 00:36:15.931
I have no need
to pay that is not equal

636
00:36:16.058 --> 00:36:19.146
to those of whom
I will prove myself equal.

637
00:36:19.607 --> 00:36:20.273
Sir.

638
00:36:22.069 --> 00:36:23.363
God save the King.

639
00:36:29.543 --> 00:36:30.711
[uplifting music]

640
00:36:33.801 --> 00:36:35.721
[Sally] I can't say
red becomes you. George.

641
00:36:36.223 --> 00:36:37.390
You don't think so?

642
00:36:37.516 --> 00:36:40.355
Well. even if I did.
I wouldn't say.

643
00:36:40.898 --> 00:36:42.275
[Sally] Thank you for
your letters.

644
00:36:43.111 --> 00:36:44.615
I read them all ten times over.

645
00:36:46.619 --> 00:36:50.208
At the river's fork. the world
widened as though God himself

646
00:36:50.333 --> 00:36:53.924
had drawn back the curtain
and whispered. "Begin."

647
00:36:56.138 --> 00:36:57.933
These are not surveyor’s notes.

648
00:36:58.058 --> 00:37:02.482
No. You love the frontier the
way poets love their first muse.

649
00:37:02.733 --> 00:37:03.736
Why?

650
00:37:04.361 --> 00:37:07.995
It loved me first. I guess.
Offered fairness.

651
00:37:08.495 --> 00:37:09.162
Fairness?

652
00:37:09.287 --> 00:37:12.880
Yes. Because the frontier is
new. wild. unclaimed.

653
00:37:13.421 --> 00:37:15.759
Vast enough to outrun
the old ways.

654
00:37:15.884 --> 00:37:19.977
And old rules? Like dowries and
fathers who barter daughters.

655
00:37:20.102 --> 00:37:24.401
Rules that say a man is measured
by ancestors you never met.

656
00:37:27.490 --> 00:37:30.581
Do you ever fear of
choosing incorrectly?

657
00:37:31.499 --> 00:37:35.215
That the path you seek might
vanish if you hesitate?

658
00:37:35.799 --> 00:37:39.097
The fear of not being able
to choose is worse.

659
00:37:41.269 --> 00:37:42.940
My fear is choosing.

660
00:37:43.732 --> 00:37:46.572
Then being told it was never
my choice to begin with.

661
00:37:46.697 --> 00:37:49.578
Then what would your choice be?

662
00:38:02.102 --> 00:38:06.151
If we were to follow
the river west. just you and I.

663
00:38:07.780 --> 00:38:09.868
what would we call that life?

664
00:38:11.454 --> 00:38:15.170
Wild. Beautiful.

665
00:38:15.879 --> 00:38:19.011
Dangerous. But. but free.

666
00:38:22.601 --> 00:38:25.608
I yearn for the
courage I see in you.

667
00:38:26.318 --> 00:38:29.239
And I. for the grace
you carry with ease.

668
00:38:32.788 --> 00:38:34.793
I should be getting back.

669
00:38:38.216 --> 00:38:39.009
Where?

670
00:38:39.635 --> 00:38:42.725
Another party.
Another performance.

671
00:38:46.106 --> 00:38:47.359
My solemn duty.

672
00:38:54.122 --> 00:38:56.378
[romantic music]

673
00:39:08.819 --> 00:39:10.238
[adventurous music]

674
00:39:27.355 --> 00:39:29.442
Congratulations on your first
command. Major.

675
00:39:29.568 --> 00:39:33.994
An army of outlaws.
debtors. slaves. and...

676
00:39:34.955 --> 00:39:35.706
[chuckles] well. patriots.

677
00:39:35.831 --> 00:39:37.585
Got any rum in
those carts?

678
00:39:37.710 --> 00:39:38.921
Only what’s rationed.

679
00:39:39.046 --> 00:39:40.549
Well. then ration us some.

680
00:39:40.799 --> 00:39:42.135
Back in line. Frisk.

681
00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:43.430
[Henry] Ain't no line.

682
00:39:43.806 --> 00:39:45.643
That snake trail is
the best we can do.

683
00:39:45.768 --> 00:39:47.605
It ain’t wide enough
for the carts.

684
00:39:47.730 --> 00:39:48.774
We should leave ‘em.

685
00:39:48.899 --> 00:39:50.986
Then how would we carry the rum?

686
00:39:51.111 --> 00:39:52.072
Fair point.

687
00:39:53.534 --> 00:39:54.409
Tucker!

688
00:39:54.995 --> 00:39:55.746
Yes. sir.

689
00:39:55.871 --> 00:39:57.708
We’ll camp here for the night.

690
00:39:57.833 --> 00:40:00.714
Ride ahead.
Make sure the road is clear.

691
00:40:07.603 --> 00:40:08.856
[Christopher] I wake
up at midnight.

692
00:40:08.981 --> 00:40:11.109
George is staring
into the woods.

693
00:40:11.234 --> 00:40:13.071
Propped against a tree.
musket in his lap.

694
00:40:13.448 --> 00:40:15.828
He says he's
been keepin' watch.

695
00:40:16.161 --> 00:40:17.623
You scared of the dark. George?

696
00:40:18.040 --> 00:40:19.920
George. you remember?

697
00:40:20.045 --> 00:40:21.379
[men laugh]

698
00:40:21.674 --> 00:40:22.800
Another love letter.

699
00:40:22.925 --> 00:40:24.344
[laughing]

700
00:40:25.055 --> 00:40:26.975
[Christopher] That woman's
gonna make you soft.

701
00:40:27.350 --> 00:40:29.021
[horse neighs]

702
00:40:33.989 --> 00:40:35.492
It's Tucker's horse.

703
00:40:46.724 --> 00:40:47.850
[muskets cracking]

704
00:40:49.269 --> 00:40:50.355
Van Braam.

705
00:40:52.568 --> 00:40:54.487
What business do you have with us?

706
00:40:55.490 --> 00:40:58.036
We have no conflict with you.

707
00:40:58.330 --> 00:41:00.333
We are only here...

708
00:41:00.333 --> 00:41:02.004
To speak to the French.

709
00:41:03.882 --> 00:41:05.260
We meet again.

710
00:41:07.681 --> 00:41:09.560
I'm Tanacharison.

711
00:41:09.685 --> 00:41:11.229
Of the Seneca nation.

712
00:41:11.354 --> 00:41:13.360
You ride on land we call home.

713
00:41:13.485 --> 00:41:16.992
The Governor assures
me you're willing to aid us.

714
00:41:17.826 --> 00:41:21.499
Many Indians are aligned
with the French. Why aren't you?

715
00:41:21.625 --> 00:41:23.045
I know their nature.

716
00:41:24.339 --> 00:41:25.843
And their intentions.

717
00:41:26.929 --> 00:41:28.013
What are yours?

718
00:41:28.305 --> 00:41:29.808
To demand they leave.

719
00:41:30.143 --> 00:41:31.645
And when they do not?

720
00:41:32.480 --> 00:41:33.441
That's not my decision.

721
00:41:33.567 --> 00:41:34.317
And yet you are here.

722
00:41:34.442 --> 00:41:37.074
Yes. and I would
greatly appreciate

723
00:41:37.199 --> 00:41:39.119
any help you
could give us.

724
00:41:45.005 --> 00:41:46.424
What are you called?

725
00:41:48.053 --> 00:41:48.722
George.

726
00:41:50.518 --> 00:41:52.312
Major George Washington.

727
00:42:04.920 --> 00:42:07.425
The French fort is
a day from here.

728
00:42:09.597 --> 00:42:10.849
We can take you.

729
00:42:11.517 --> 00:42:13.186
[ominous music]

730
00:42:43.080 --> 00:42:44.625
Why are you here?

731
00:43:03.664 --> 00:43:06.669
Why do you hate them?

732
00:43:08.882 --> 00:43:11.094
When I was a child

733
00:43:11.094 --> 00:43:16.188
I was taken captive by the French

734
00:43:11.637 --> 00:43:13.098
[horse neighing]

735
00:43:16.229 --> 00:43:20.948
I watched them boil my father.

736
00:43:20.948 --> 00:43:24.747
And eat him.

737
00:43:31.760 --> 00:43:35.268
From the royal Governor of Virginia:

738
00:43:35.310 --> 00:43:40.529
Sir. the lands upon the Ohio River
are notoriously known

739
00:43:40.571 --> 00:43:44.411
to be the property
of the Crown of Great Britain

740
00:43:44.452 --> 00:43:47.793
that it is a matter of equal concern
and surprise to hear that a body of

741
00:43:47.835 --> 00:43:53.681
French forces are erecting fortresses
within His Majesty's dominions.

742
00:43:53.681 --> 00:43:55.098
His dominion?

743
00:43:57.312 --> 00:43:58.857
Continue.

744
00:43:59.900 --> 00:44:04.201
In the name of the King. my master.
I have sent the bearer hereof.

745
00:44:04.242 --> 00:44:05.871
Major George Washington.

746
00:44:05.913 --> 00:44:10.714
one of the Adjutants-General
of this British Dominion.

747
00:44:13.511 --> 00:44:14.972
You are the Major?

748
00:44:15.390 --> 00:44:16.725
or his aide?

749
00:44:17.185 --> 00:44:18.772
I am Major Washington.

750
00:44:22.154 --> 00:44:23.280
[speaking French]

751
00:44:23.405 --> 00:44:25.452
[men laugh]

752
00:44:29.501 --> 00:44:31.589
[speaking French]

753
00:44:39.938 --> 00:44:42.736
He's inviting
us to dine with them.

754
00:44:49.583 --> 00:44:52.756
[ominous music]

755
00:45:01.148 --> 00:45:02.860
Can we speak in private?

756
00:45:04.780 --> 00:45:06.324
[speaking French]

757
00:45:10.040 --> 00:45:13.130
He says there's no
need to leave the table.

758
00:45:13.255 --> 00:45:14.216
We are all friends here.

759
00:45:14.883 --> 00:45:16.178
[Christopher speaking
Seneca]

760
00:45:19.017 --> 00:45:20.688
Know thy enemy indeed.

761
00:45:26.406 --> 00:45:29.997
So. how is it you are a Major?

762
00:45:32.502 --> 00:45:33.671
Do you even shave?

763
00:45:33.796 --> 00:45:35.298
[men laugh]

764
00:45:36.009 --> 00:45:38.096
You have no military service.

765
00:45:38.221 --> 00:45:39.349
Is it true?

766
00:45:40.350 --> 00:45:42.145
Magnifique.
You are not British.

767
00:45:42.272 --> 00:45:44.484
yet they send you
to speak for them.

768
00:45:45.277 --> 00:45:47.072
Why do you think that is?

769
00:45:48.325 --> 00:45:52.585
So that when you fail.
they'll have someone to blame.

770
00:45:55.005 --> 00:45:58.470
The King emphatically demands
you leave the Ohio country.

771
00:45:59.807 --> 00:46:02.019
and the territories altogether.

772
00:46:03.146 --> 00:46:06.529
This land has long been
claimed by the British Crown.

773
00:46:06.654 --> 00:46:08.490
And when was this?

774
00:46:08.616 --> 00:46:09.618
[in French] When?

775
00:46:10.493 --> 00:46:12.457
When did they claim it?

776
00:46:13.751 --> 00:46:15.253
You must withdraw.

777
00:46:15.378 --> 00:46:17.968
Because you
think you own this land?

778
00:46:19.972 --> 00:46:21.892
Who does own this land.

779
00:46:22.017 --> 00:46:24.231
if not the one who has
the will to tame it?

780
00:46:24.356 --> 00:46:25.901
[fists banging on the table]

781
00:46:27.445 --> 00:46:28.864
[indistinct chatter]

782
00:46:40.513 --> 00:46:42.350
I accept your message.

783
00:46:43.435 --> 00:46:45.188
You have delivered it.

784
00:46:46.149 --> 00:46:47.067
Now go.

785
00:46:49.197 --> 00:46:50.993
The King demands a reply.

786
00:46:57.045 --> 00:47:00.343
Then tell your King
we have claimed it.

787
00:47:02.180 --> 00:47:03.851
We will never leave.

788
00:47:04.645 --> 00:47:06.940
Then we will force you to leave.

789
00:47:07.985 --> 00:47:09.154
Oh.

790
00:47:12.200 --> 00:47:14.707
You do not want to start a war.

791
00:47:19.758 --> 00:47:22.137
Take your pet savage and go.

792
00:47:25.896 --> 00:47:27.399
[tense music]

793
00:47:31.489 --> 00:47:33.326
[George] Camp 15 miles
south of here.

794
00:47:33.493 --> 00:47:35.372
I’m going to ride ahead
and deliver the message.

795
00:47:35.497 --> 00:47:36.667
Should we send a scout?

796
00:47:36.792 --> 00:47:38.921
I'm the fastest scout we have.

797
00:47:39.046 --> 00:47:41.134
[ominous music]

798
00:48:05.432 --> 00:48:06.309
[door opens]

799
00:48:06.434 --> 00:48:07.394
Major.

800
00:48:08.772 --> 00:48:11.820
You will deliver
this ultimatum at once.

801
00:48:14.409 --> 00:48:16.664
The French spit in my face.

802
00:48:17.122 --> 00:48:18.333
Governor. with respect.
could you clarify--

803
00:48:18.458 --> 00:48:20.295
Transcribe all you have.
so I can report this

804
00:48:20.420 --> 00:48:22.551
to the council in the morning.

805
00:48:23.636 --> 00:48:24.555
Very well.

806
00:48:25.639 --> 00:48:27.392
Grant me one night’s rest
and fresh mounts.

807
00:48:27.520 --> 00:48:28.854
I’ve ridden
300 miles to--

808
00:48:28.979 --> 00:48:32.530
You will rest when
His Majesty's frontier rests.

809
00:48:32.655 --> 00:48:33.864
Before dawn. you'll present a

810
00:48:33.989 --> 00:48:35.659
full transcription
of your journal.

811
00:48:35.784 --> 00:48:38.498
Maps. strength estimates.
every scratch of observation.

812
00:48:38.624 --> 00:48:41.755
for the council's brief
at ten o'clock. Understood?

813
00:48:41.880 --> 00:48:42.633
Understood. sir.

814
00:48:42.758 --> 00:48:43.634
Good.

815
00:48:43.842 --> 00:48:45.889
Now go and prove
the Crown correct

816
00:48:46.014 --> 00:48:48.351
in placing
trust in a provincial.

817
00:48:52.945 --> 00:48:55.741
This is a dangerous escalation.
George.

818
00:48:56.785 --> 00:48:58.622
You are to deliver this?

819
00:49:00.042 --> 00:49:01.920
I've been ordered
to deliver this.

820
00:49:02.045 --> 00:49:03.423
You volunteered.

821
00:49:07.683 --> 00:49:08.350
No.

822
00:49:09.184 --> 00:49:11.023
- No. perhaps I can speak--
- No. no.

823
00:49:11.148 --> 00:49:12.776
This is the moment
I've been waiting for.

824
00:49:12.901 --> 00:49:14.905
I don't think it is. George.

825
00:49:17.325 --> 00:49:19.790
Why has no one else volunteered?

826
00:49:21.251 --> 00:49:24.758
Why does no British
officer lead this expedition?

827
00:49:29.392 --> 00:49:31.271
They’re using you. George.

828
00:49:31.730 --> 00:49:35.195
As a proxy.
To claim land for them.

829
00:49:36.198 --> 00:49:39.454
If you succeed.
they will rob you of the glory.

830
00:49:39.580 --> 00:49:41.959
If you fail. they'll have
a colonial to blame.

831
00:49:42.084 --> 00:49:42.961
Then I will not fail.

832
00:49:43.086 --> 00:49:44.673
If you do.
it could start a war.

833
00:49:44.798 --> 00:49:46.844
Thank you for your trust in me.

834
00:49:46.969 --> 00:49:48.681
That's not what I meant.

835
00:49:49.432 --> 00:49:52.856
I will claim it. and
I will earn their respect.

836
00:49:53.106 --> 00:49:55.819
That is what you
taught me. is it not?

837
00:49:55.944 --> 00:49:57.908
Besides. this is a new world.

838
00:49:58.075 --> 00:49:58.951
A new world?

839
00:49:59.452 --> 00:50:00.663
The soil may be new.

840
00:50:00.788 --> 00:50:02.876
but it’s owners still write
their ledgers in old ink.

841
00:50:03.001 --> 00:50:04.211
Let them write.

842
00:50:08.804 --> 00:50:13.647
You're betting your life on a
system designed to deny you.

843
00:50:14.567 --> 00:50:17.655
Every triumph you have
will be chalked up to luck.

844
00:50:17.781 --> 00:50:21.163
or the Native allies
or the British themselves.

845
00:50:21.371 --> 00:50:22.330
Never you.

846
00:50:22.455 --> 00:50:24.042
So I should stay here.

847
00:50:24.167 --> 00:50:27.926
mind the crops and live quietly
because I was born quietly?

848
00:50:28.051 --> 00:50:29.471
Do nothing with my life?

849
00:50:29.597 --> 00:50:31.183
Better alive and quiet

850
00:50:32.017 --> 00:50:33.771
than dead and forgotten
in the Alleghenies.

851
00:50:33.896 --> 00:50:35.023
You sound like mother.

852
00:50:35.148 --> 00:50:36.109
I speak the truth.

853
00:50:36.234 --> 00:50:37.821
[laughs] Well I would rather die
unknown than live

854
00:50:37.946 --> 00:50:40.075
believing the world’s
measure of me is fixed.

855
00:50:40.200 --> 00:50:42.204
That...that is pride.

856
00:50:42.329 --> 00:50:44.459
No. that is faith in what a man
can forge with his own hands.

857
00:50:44.585 --> 00:50:46.463
You cannot forge
your way into their system.

858
00:50:46.589 --> 00:50:47.297
And why not?

859
00:50:47.422 --> 00:50:49.009
Because that is not
the way the world works.

860
00:50:49.134 --> 00:50:50.387
Then someone should remake it.

861
00:50:50.513 --> 00:50:51.724
[Lawrence coughs]

862
00:50:55.188 --> 00:50:58.654
George. you
cannot change these things.

863
00:51:00.824 --> 00:51:03.330
You may well die trying.

864
00:51:06.629 --> 00:51:07.295
George--

865
00:51:07.420 --> 00:51:09.718
I wish you believed in me.

866
00:51:13.601 --> 00:51:15.729
[coughing]

867
00:51:21.825 --> 00:51:24.496
[soft string music]

868
00:51:24.623 --> 00:51:26.166
[indistinct chatter]

869
00:51:49.421 --> 00:51:50.508
[Sally] Major Washington.

870
00:51:50.633 --> 00:51:52.761
I thought you were leading
your men to the frontier.

871
00:51:52.886 --> 00:51:54.014
Tomorrow I am.

872
00:51:54.139 --> 00:51:55.893
But I have returned
on an urgent matter.

873
00:51:56.018 --> 00:51:57.354
I'll go back in the morning.

874
00:51:57.521 --> 00:51:59.818
But. tonight. I am here for you.

875
00:51:59.943 --> 00:52:01.321
[inaudible whispers]

876
00:52:02.489 --> 00:52:04.995
George. there is no
fairness here.

877
00:52:05.120 --> 00:52:07.625
Miss Cary—may I
have this dance?

878
00:52:08.001 --> 00:52:09.545
[string music plays]

879
00:52:09.963 --> 00:52:10.923
Yes. Major.

880
00:52:48.081 --> 00:52:51.589
George. I see
you found a tailor.

881
00:52:51.880 --> 00:52:52.798
Yes.

882
00:52:52.965 --> 00:52:55.137
Tonight I wear
His Majesty's commission.

883
00:52:55.262 --> 00:52:56.849
At dawn. I am
to lead 150 soldiers

884
00:52:56.974 --> 00:52:59.186
to demand the
French leave our land.

885
00:52:59.311 --> 00:53:02.651
Well. our land. to be precise.

886
00:53:03.111 --> 00:53:05.949
And this is not exactly
His Majesty's commission.

887
00:53:06.074 --> 00:53:08.706
Your uniform. however.
crimson. still prints colonial.

888
00:53:08.831 --> 00:53:09.540
William.

889
00:53:09.750 --> 00:53:12.755
It is a point I make
intentionally. Sally.

890
00:53:12.963 --> 00:53:15.511
I fear for you. George.

891
00:53:16.386 --> 00:53:19.770
And I question
our Governor's decision.

892
00:53:20.896 --> 00:53:24.236
If the situation
with the French is so dire.

893
00:53:24.361 --> 00:53:25.447
why would they not

894
00:53:25.573 --> 00:53:28.328
send professional
soldiers of the Crown?

895
00:53:28.453 --> 00:53:30.040
Because I volunteered.

896
00:53:31.041 --> 00:53:33.506
And if you care so much.
why didn't you?

897
00:53:33.631 --> 00:53:36.009
Because I have an estate to run.

898
00:53:37.012 --> 00:53:39.266
And I have a fortune to manage.

899
00:53:39.935 --> 00:53:41.897
And people depend on me.

900
00:53:43.609 --> 00:53:44.610
But...

901
00:53:45.738 --> 00:53:50.748
I can send along two of
my best slaves. Charles and Sam.

902
00:53:51.373 --> 00:53:55.465
Charles knows horses better than
most grooms in Virginia.

903
00:53:55.674 --> 00:53:59.389
Well. I wouldn't want
to deprive you of their labor.

904
00:53:59.557 --> 00:54:00.976
We have plenty.

905
00:54:01.309 --> 00:54:02.605
[Lord Fairfax] Major
Washington.

906
00:54:04.943 --> 00:54:08.366
Congratulations on
your rank and assignment.

907
00:54:08.617 --> 00:54:10.078
An astonishing rise.

908
00:54:11.163 --> 00:54:12.249
Thank you. sir.

909
00:54:12.625 --> 00:54:16.381
So. what think you of our young
William and Sally?

910
00:54:16.507 --> 00:54:17.175
Yes.

911
00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:19.890
Do they not make a.
a handsome couple?

912
00:54:20.516 --> 00:54:23.564
We are gathered
here to celebrate this.

913
00:54:23.981 --> 00:54:26.779
Their betrothal
is scarcely a week old.

914
00:54:28.406 --> 00:54:29.407
Uh...

915
00:54:29.533 --> 00:54:30.828
Indeed they do.

916
00:54:30.953 --> 00:54:32.080
Splendid!

917
00:54:32.205 --> 00:54:34.126
Now. may I propose a toast?

918
00:54:35.128 --> 00:54:38.552
To Major Washington—
who rides at first light...

919
00:54:38.677 --> 00:54:40.430
[speech fades behind music]

920
00:54:44.647 --> 00:54:46.233
[low rumbling sound]

921
00:54:46.399 --> 00:54:47.611
[Fairfax] Major Washington.

922
00:54:49.865 --> 00:54:51.326
William. Miss Cary.

923
00:54:51.870 --> 00:54:52.705
Forgive the stir.

924
00:54:52.830 --> 00:54:56.044
I look forward to returning
worthy of your investment...

925
00:54:56.169 --> 00:54:57.673
and your care.

926
00:54:59.426 --> 00:55:01.724
[soft music]

927
00:55:10.616 --> 00:55:12.119
[George] Act on the defensive

928
00:55:12.578 --> 00:55:15.417
But if any attempts are made to
disrupt our work or settlements.

929
00:55:15.543 --> 00:55:16.962
restrain all such offenders.

930
00:55:17.087 --> 00:55:20.761
and make prisoners of.
or kill and destroy. them.

931
00:55:22.097 --> 00:55:23.433
Well. that’s clear as mud.

932
00:55:23.559 --> 00:55:24.810
He cannot be serious.

933
00:55:24.935 --> 00:55:26.021
“Destroy them?”

934
00:55:26.146 --> 00:55:28.025
If it’s war he wants.
it's best to reinforce us

935
00:55:28.150 --> 00:55:29.361
with proper British soldiers.

936
00:55:29.486 --> 00:55:30.614
We ain't here to fight.

937
00:55:30.739 --> 00:55:31.532
Then why are you?

938
00:55:31.657 --> 00:55:32.535
To get paid.

939
00:55:32.743 --> 00:55:33.537
This is our duty.

940
00:55:33.662 --> 00:55:34.872
No. it ain't.

941
00:55:35.624 --> 00:55:38.170
We delivered his little letter.
We should leave.

942
00:55:38.295 --> 00:55:39.214
You will not.

943
00:55:39.965 --> 00:55:42.888
Or I will have
you flogged as a deserter.

944
00:55:44.016 --> 00:55:45.853
Now. we didn't
sign up for no war.

945
00:55:45.978 --> 00:55:47.480
You put on the coat!

946
00:55:48.356 --> 00:55:49.568
You took an oath.

947
00:55:50.904 --> 00:55:53.241
You have a duty. as do I.

948
00:55:56.750 --> 00:55:59.129
If this goes wrong.
he’ll blame Virginia.

949
00:55:59.254 --> 00:56:01.675
[George] Dinwiddie speaks
for the Crown.

950
00:56:03.178 --> 00:56:06.644
It's decided. This is a direct
order and we will obey it.

951
00:56:06.770 --> 00:56:07.980
It's not direct at all.

952
00:56:08.105 --> 00:56:10.067
Then your gods have
delivered you to war.

953
00:56:10.736 --> 00:56:11.737
It is not our intent.

954
00:56:11.864 --> 00:56:13.659
[Tucker] I found
their encampment.

955
00:56:14.910 --> 00:56:17.082
It’s much further south.
Much closer.

956
00:56:17.207 --> 00:56:17.916
How close?

957
00:56:18.291 --> 00:56:19.086
Five miles.

958
00:56:19.502 --> 00:56:22.092
[Tanacharison] He searches for
land to build another fort.

959
00:56:22.217 --> 00:56:25.641
To demand you abandon
the land he calls his own.

960
00:56:26.894 --> 00:56:27.978
Take me to him.

961
00:56:29.815 --> 00:56:32.237
A simple
reconnaissance. Agreed?

962
00:56:42.007 --> 00:56:44.512
[tense music]

963
00:57:11.607 --> 00:57:13.193
[Tanacharison] Drunk with
his own pride.

964
00:57:13.318 --> 00:57:16.910
He defies you and your King
by traveling this far.

965
00:57:22.004 --> 00:57:23.296
What will you do?

966
00:57:29.017 --> 00:57:30.437
Hold your ground.

967
00:57:31.564 --> 00:57:33.150
I'll tell them once
again to leave.

968
00:57:33.275 --> 00:57:35.447
What will you do
when they refuse?

969
00:57:35.573 --> 00:57:36.615
-Pray they--
-[gunshot]

970
00:57:42.085 --> 00:57:43.504
Who fired that shot?

971
00:57:45.132 --> 00:57:46.301
[gunshot]

972
00:57:49.266 --> 00:57:50.686
Hold your ground!

973
00:57:50.811 --> 00:57:51.645
Hold your ground!

974
00:57:51.770 --> 00:57:52.856
[yelling in French]

975
00:57:57.157 --> 00:57:58.534
[indian whoops and yells]

976
00:58:01.123 --> 00:58:02.500
[gunshots]

977
00:58:03.712 --> 00:58:05.423
[yelling in French]

978
00:58:19.034 --> 00:58:20.243
Forward!

979
00:58:26.965 --> 00:58:29.137
[yelling]

980
00:58:29.262 --> 00:58:31.934
[gunshots]

981
00:58:39.074 --> 00:58:40.158
Hold your fire!

982
00:58:40.661 --> 00:58:41.745
Hold your fire!

983
00:58:41.870 --> 00:58:42.956
Prisoners only!

984
00:58:43.081 --> 00:58:44.376
Prisoners only!

985
00:58:44.501 --> 00:58:45.168
Prisoners--

986
00:58:45.293 --> 00:58:47.508
[yelling]
[gunshot]

987
00:58:47.633 --> 00:58:49.094
[sigh]

988
00:58:49.219 --> 00:58:50.303
[sound of heartbeat]

989
00:58:53.771 --> 00:58:55.608
[sound of heartbeat]

990
00:58:55.733 --> 00:58:57.360
[soldier yells]

991
00:58:59.657 --> 00:59:02.162
[yelling]
[gunshots]

992
00:59:07.590 --> 00:59:09.802
We should have killed everyone of you.

993
00:59:15.814 --> 00:59:17.901
Thou art not yet dead. my father.

994
00:59:22.536 --> 00:59:23.787
-Wait!
-[Jumonville groans]

995
00:59:24.247 --> 00:59:25.332
Wait!

996
00:59:27.002 --> 00:59:28.882
[indian whoops and cheers]

997
00:59:33.516 --> 00:59:36.396
[George] I do not know who
fired that first shot.

998
00:59:36.814 --> 00:59:38.986
but in light of
these unfortunate events.

999
00:59:39.111 --> 00:59:42.701
I fear a war with the
French is indeed imminent.

1000
00:59:43.577 --> 00:59:47.711
We are building a fort and
taking up a defensive position.

1001
00:59:47.836 --> 00:59:49.757
In the spirit
of mutual benefit.

1002
00:59:49.882 --> 00:59:53.263
please send reinforcements
to aid our endeavor.

1003
00:59:55.978 --> 00:59:57.397
[David] Hey.
why don't we arm them?

1004
00:59:57.690 --> 00:59:59.902
We need all the men we can get.

1005
01:00:01.238 --> 01:00:02.783
They might shoot us.

1006
01:00:03.701 --> 01:00:04.787
Wouldn't you?

1007
01:00:05.495 --> 01:00:06.456
Fair point.

1008
01:00:06.915 --> 01:00:08.085
-Gist!
-Yep.

1009
01:00:10.841 --> 01:00:12.761
Permission to speak my mind.

1010
01:00:12.886 --> 01:00:13.931
Never stopped you?

1011
01:00:14.056 --> 01:00:15.057
[sarcastic laugh]

1012
01:00:15.726 --> 01:00:17.646
Building this fort too low.

1013
01:00:17.980 --> 01:00:19.399
What do you mean?

1014
01:00:19.942 --> 01:00:21.028
The walls?

1015
01:00:22.573 --> 01:00:24.117
No. not the walls--

1016
01:00:24.242 --> 01:00:26.872
This here. this is a
dry lake bed.

1017
01:00:27.625 --> 01:00:30.503
One good rain. it’ll flood out.

1018
01:00:30.881 --> 01:00:34.805
Besides. I could shoot
every one of us from them trees.

1019
01:00:38.812 --> 01:00:40.776
Major know what he’s doin?

1020
01:00:44.700 --> 01:00:45.911
What you writing?

1021
01:00:46.203 --> 01:00:48.206
Another plea for reinforcements.

1022
01:00:48.749 --> 01:00:49.627
From who?

1023
01:00:50.335 --> 01:00:51.296
Colonies.

1024
01:00:52.675 --> 01:00:55.889
Pennsylvania don't care
about Virginia's problems.

1025
01:00:56.014 --> 01:00:59.021
The French are the
concern of all. Agreed?

1026
01:01:00.899 --> 01:01:02.861
This area lies awfully low.

1027
01:01:03.737 --> 01:01:05.616
The forest gives us cover.

1028
01:01:06.201 --> 01:01:07.495
The great meadows offer
plenty of space

1029
01:01:07.621 --> 01:01:09.542
and a clear view
of any oncoming threats.

1030
01:01:09.667 --> 01:01:11.503
If they attack.
it'll be from the front.

1031
01:01:11.629 --> 01:01:15.302
Or. we'll be easy
targets. when the fort floods.

1032
01:01:18.642 --> 01:01:20.478
Well. Gist. what would
you have me do?

1033
01:01:20.604 --> 01:01:21.815
Major Washington.

1034
01:01:22.526 --> 01:01:23.485
The King's troops.

1035
01:01:23.611 --> 01:01:24.738
What about them?

1036
01:01:25.238 --> 01:01:26.659
[Tucker] They're here.

1037
01:01:49.329 --> 01:01:50.706
Where's Washington?

1038
01:01:50.999 --> 01:01:52.167
I am Major Washington.

1039
01:01:52.334 --> 01:01:53.045
[scoffs]

1040
01:01:53.420 --> 01:01:54.923
Captain James Mackay.

1041
01:01:56.093 --> 01:01:58.305
Orders from Governor Dinwiddie.

1042
01:01:59.767 --> 01:02:02.648
We are here to reinforce
the Virginia Regiment

1043
01:02:02.773 --> 01:02:06.363
and deal with this...
situation you’ve created.

1044
01:02:07.616 --> 01:02:10.287
French and Indian soldiers.
Professional soldiers.

1045
01:02:10.412 --> 01:02:11.999
Are nearly upon us.

1046
01:02:12.124 --> 01:02:14.044
Over a thousand in total.

1047
01:02:14.171 --> 01:02:17.342
They are commanded by
Louis Coulon de Villiers.

1048
01:02:17.467 --> 01:02:20.934
Brother to Joseph Coulon
de Villiers de Jumonville.

1049
01:02:21.059 --> 01:02:23.230
The man who you killed.

1050
01:02:28.156 --> 01:02:30.243
This letter says Colonel
Joshua Fry is in command.

1051
01:02:30.368 --> 01:02:31.872
Oh. the boy can read.

1052
01:02:32.247 --> 01:02:33.125
Where is he?

1053
01:02:33.250 --> 01:02:34.252
Dead.

1054
01:02:34.837 --> 01:02:37.968
Fell from his horse two
days ago and broke his neck.

1055
01:02:38.093 --> 01:02:41.975
You are to assume his rank
as Colonel. Mr. Washington.

1056
01:02:43.896 --> 01:02:45.273
[George] Well then. welcome.

1057
01:02:45.608 --> 01:02:47.863
We need all
the help we can get.

1058
01:02:47.988 --> 01:02:49.700
I do not take orders from you.

1059
01:02:49.825 --> 01:02:50.826
But...

1060
01:02:51.369 --> 01:02:53.248
you said I was to
assume the rank is Colonel.

1061
01:02:53.373 --> 01:02:55.002
My commission is royal.

1062
01:02:55.252 --> 01:02:58.258
You could be a general and I
wouldn't have to listen to you.

1063
01:02:58.383 --> 01:02:59.176
Praise God.

1064
01:03:00.262 --> 01:03:03.686
Now. what do
you call this... fort?

1065
01:03:04.522 --> 01:03:06.567
Well. it was made by necessity.

1066
01:03:06.692 --> 01:03:08.070
So I think
that's a fitting name.

1067
01:03:08.195 --> 01:03:09.196
Mmm.

1068
01:03:09.865 --> 01:03:12.160
We will camp 100 yards
to the front.

1069
01:03:12.285 --> 01:03:15.375
No doubt the French
will engage us there.

1070
01:03:15.543 --> 01:03:17.129
Colonel.

1071
01:03:17.337 --> 01:03:18.340
Van Braam.

1072
01:03:23.433 --> 01:03:24.352
[Mackay] The boy can read.

1073
01:03:24.477 --> 01:03:25.563
[Mackay chuckles]

1074
01:03:29.863 --> 01:03:31.867
[water splashing]

1075
01:03:33.245 --> 01:03:34.998
[thunder booms]

1076
01:03:51.824 --> 01:03:53.201
How's the progress?

1077
01:03:53.410 --> 01:03:56.166
Ditch is taking in water
faster than we can throw it.

1078
01:03:56.291 --> 01:03:59.004
I say. this keeps up.

1079
01:03:59.212 --> 01:04:03.013
I’ll commission my men to
construct a Royal Navy.

1080
01:04:03.138 --> 01:04:04.222
Keep trying.

1081
01:04:07.104 --> 01:04:08.857
I could shoot you
from the trees.

1082
01:04:08.982 --> 01:04:10.819
The French won’t fire
from the trees.

1083
01:04:10.944 --> 01:04:14.953
They’ll assemble in open fields.
To fight with honor.

1084
01:04:15.162 --> 01:04:17.290
You call this
land the New World?

1085
01:04:17.415 --> 01:04:19.252
Yet you live by the old ways.

1086
01:04:19.377 --> 01:04:21.383
They will lead you to death.

1087
01:04:21.592 --> 01:04:23.721
Any recruits among the Shawnee?

1088
01:04:23.846 --> 01:04:24.515
No.

1089
01:04:24.640 --> 01:04:26.560
What about the Delaware
or the Mingo?

1090
01:04:26.685 --> 01:04:29.064
No. Some have
even joined the French.

1091
01:04:29.189 --> 01:04:30.651
None will aid you.

1092
01:04:32.655 --> 01:04:34.032
Neither will we.

1093
01:04:35.035 --> 01:04:36.413
You will not leave!

1094
01:04:38.375 --> 01:04:40.045
Your vengeance started this.

1095
01:04:40.170 --> 01:04:42.049
And your stubbornness
will be the end of it.

1096
01:04:42.174 --> 01:04:43.802
The French are cowards.

1097
01:04:43.927 --> 01:04:45.514
The British are fools.

1098
01:04:45.639 --> 01:04:47.643
You do not
know how to fight here.

1099
01:04:47.768 --> 01:04:50.190
I was born here on
this land. as were you.

1100
01:04:50.315 --> 01:04:52.695
Can we not
fight for it together?

1101
01:04:53.405 --> 01:04:57.287
This land
does not belong to you.

1102
01:04:57.412 --> 01:04:59.291
While you kill each other.

1103
01:05:00.002 --> 01:05:01.589
we wait to reclaim it.

1104
01:05:04.009 --> 01:05:07.140
[Christopher] George. you made
the wrong choice of ground.

1105
01:05:07.474 --> 01:05:11.567
Admit it. That's it. It's
alright. it's alright. Admit it.

1106
01:05:11.692 --> 01:05:13.028
Our supplies are exhausted.

1107
01:05:13.153 --> 01:05:15.157
We’ve two days' rations at best.

1108
01:05:15.282 --> 01:05:19.247
Move camp and save the men.

1109
01:05:22.420 --> 01:05:24.132
We will stand our ground.

1110
01:05:31.398 --> 01:05:33.026
Any sign of the French?

1111
01:05:33.443 --> 01:05:35.531
Nothing. No doubt the arrival
of actual soldiers

1112
01:05:35.656 --> 01:05:37.200
put a stop
to their advancements.

1113
01:05:37.325 --> 01:05:41.041
But listen. my men are
camping in what is now a swamp.

1114
01:05:41.166 --> 01:05:42.711
What do you want me to do?

1115
01:05:42.836 --> 01:05:44.006
Find solid ground.

1116
01:05:44.131 --> 01:05:46.679
Or better yet. an
experienced commander.

1117
01:05:46.804 --> 01:05:48.807
Are you
challenging my authority?

1118
01:05:48.932 --> 01:05:50.435
[scoffs] You have no authority.

1119
01:05:50.603 --> 01:05:51.772
-[gunshot]
-[Mackay grunts]

1120
01:05:58.368 --> 01:06:01.374
Trees! They're in the trees!
Take cover!

1121
01:06:01.499 --> 01:06:02.751
-[horse neighs]
-[gunshots boom]

1122
01:06:06.802 --> 01:06:08.138
[yelling and gunshots]

1123
01:06:09.264 --> 01:06:10.433
Move. move.

1124
01:06:10.643 --> 01:06:11.520
Go. go. go.

1125
01:06:11.645 --> 01:06:12.437
Grab a musket.

1126
01:06:13.273 --> 01:06:14.902
Move. move. move. move!

1127
01:06:15.819 --> 01:06:16.780
[George] Hold the line.

1128
01:06:17.197 --> 01:06:18.491
Form a line on me.

1129
01:06:18.617 --> 01:06:20.579
A line? Yeah. a smart idea.

1130
01:06:24.713 --> 01:06:25.714
Fire!

1131
01:06:30.098 --> 01:06:31.644
They’re firing from all sides.

1132
01:06:31.769 --> 01:06:33.271
To the front with me!

1133
01:06:35.358 --> 01:06:37.571
Form up! On me. on me.

1134
01:06:40.452 --> 01:06:41.119
Christopher.

1135
01:06:41.244 --> 01:06:41.914
Yeah?

1136
01:06:42.330 --> 01:06:44.585
Divide the men. Keep 50 in
the fort and fire to the trees.

1137
01:06:44.712 --> 01:06:46.549
50 won’t fit in the fort.
it’s flooded out.

1138
01:06:46.674 --> 01:06:47.758
As many as you can. then.

1139
01:06:47.883 --> 01:06:49.847
All right men on me!
Move. move. move. move.

1140
01:06:49.972 --> 01:06:51.306
Everyone to the front line.

1141
01:06:51.433 --> 01:06:52.100
Present.

1142
01:06:53.061 --> 01:06:54.062
Fire!

1143
01:06:56.569 --> 01:06:58.405
[Henry] George. cannons!

1144
01:07:03.456 --> 01:07:04.835
[David] George.
what's the plan. here?

1145
01:07:05.460 --> 01:07:06.505
Second rank!

1146
01:07:06.630 --> 01:07:07.840
Forward!

1147
01:07:09.510 --> 01:07:10.513
Present!

1148
01:07:12.891 --> 01:07:13.769
Make ready!

1149
01:07:14.269 --> 01:07:15.438
Fire!

1150
01:07:17.818 --> 01:07:19.237
[bullets whizzing]

1151
01:07:21.744 --> 01:07:23.036
Fire!

1152
01:07:28.173 --> 01:07:29.633
[men yell]

1153
01:07:32.598 --> 01:07:33.475
Retreat!

1154
01:07:34.602 --> 01:07:35.854
Back to the fort.

1155
01:07:46.919 --> 01:07:49.006
Back to the fort. Get inside!

1156
01:07:56.605 --> 01:07:57.523
[George] Move!

1157
01:07:57.648 --> 01:08:00.237
Get inside! Get inside!

1158
01:08:01.071 --> 01:08:01.740
[George] Move!

1159
01:08:03.827 --> 01:08:05.914
[men yelling]

1160
01:08:09.171 --> 01:08:10.716
Come on. Get in!

1161
01:08:11.719 --> 01:08:12.636
Get in there!

1162
01:08:13.639 --> 01:08:14.431
[George] Get inside!

1163
01:08:15.601 --> 01:08:16.268
Inside!

1164
01:08:16.434 --> 01:08:17.605
[Christopher] George!
George!

1165
01:08:17.730 --> 01:08:19.107
[George] Barricade the door!

1166
01:08:19.274 --> 01:08:20.193
[George] Hold!

1167
01:08:20.778 --> 01:08:22.322
-[cannon fire booms]
-[men yelling]

1168
01:08:24.409 --> 01:08:25.788
[Henry] Powder’s wet.

1169
01:08:25.913 --> 01:08:26.999
Nothing's firin'!

1170
01:08:27.124 --> 01:08:28.711
We’re sittin’ ducks here.
Colonel.

1171
01:08:28.836 --> 01:08:30.255
We keep fighting!

1172
01:08:30.380 --> 01:08:31.507
Attach bayonets!

1173
01:08:31.759 --> 01:08:33.135
The battle is lost.

1174
01:08:33.345 --> 01:08:34.513
The battle is just begun.

1175
01:08:34.638 --> 01:08:35.307
George!

1176
01:08:35.766 --> 01:08:36.810
Man your post!

1177
01:08:36.935 --> 01:08:37.728
Man your posts!

1178
01:08:37.853 --> 01:08:38.606
Washington!

1179
01:08:38.731 --> 01:08:39.565
Save your men!

1180
01:08:39.690 --> 01:08:42.404
I will not
surrender my first command.

1181
01:08:42.780 --> 01:08:43.616
Advance troops!

1182
01:08:44.157 --> 01:08:45.452
They're coming in.

1183
01:08:46.622 --> 01:08:47.748
Man your posts!

1184
01:08:52.633 --> 01:08:54.094
Hold. hold. hold!

1185
01:08:54.219 --> 01:08:55.305
[Christopher grunts]

1186
01:09:03.446 --> 01:09:04.364
Gist!

1187
01:09:04.698 --> 01:09:06.201
Gist!

1188
01:09:09.416 --> 01:09:11.044
Just breathe. just breathe.

1189
01:09:11.755 --> 01:09:12.840
Hey. hey.

1190
01:09:13.592 --> 01:09:15.303
You're gonna be okay.
You're gonna be okay.

1191
01:09:15.428 --> 01:09:19.394
Breathe. breathe.
breathe. I'm sorry.

1192
01:09:20.313 --> 01:09:22.943
[sound muffles
behind music]

1193
01:09:45.072 --> 01:09:46.114
Major!

1194
01:09:49.955 --> 01:09:50.958
Yes.

1195
01:09:52.711 --> 01:09:53.881
[George] Surrender.

1196
01:09:54.757 --> 01:09:56.635
[solemn music]

1197
01:09:59.725 --> 01:10:01.353
I'm sorry. Christopher.

1198
01:10:01.562 --> 01:10:02.898
I am so sorry!

1199
01:10:49.658 --> 01:10:50.786
[Jacob] Washington.

1200
01:10:57.257 --> 01:10:59.512
Terms are somewhat favorable.

1201
01:11:00.012 --> 01:11:02.059
It's a mutual withdrawal.

1202
01:11:02.518 --> 01:11:04.229
They take our artillery.

1203
01:11:04.479 --> 01:11:06.066
we'll remove the flag.

1204
01:11:06.734 --> 01:11:09.657
And also they demand
you take responsibility

1205
01:11:09.782 --> 01:11:12.663
for their commander's
unfortunate death.

1206
01:11:15.167 --> 01:11:16.879
We didn't start this.

1207
01:11:18.926 --> 01:11:21.722
Nobody knows
who fired that first shot.

1208
01:11:24.562 --> 01:11:26.899
I've offered myself as security.

1209
01:11:27.025 --> 01:11:28.485
I will go with them.

1210
01:11:30.616 --> 01:11:33.706
This is the best
possible outcome. Colonel.

1211
01:11:44.392 --> 01:11:45.604
Colonel.

1212
01:11:56.667 --> 01:11:58.295
What is the date today?

1213
01:11:58.922 --> 01:12:00.090
July third.

1214
01:12:00.509 --> 01:12:02.888
July the third will be
etched in my memory forever.

1215
01:12:14.703 --> 01:12:16.582
[solemn music]

1216
01:13:22.422 --> 01:13:23.632
I'm so sorry.

1217
01:13:25.302 --> 01:13:26.805
I'm so. so sorry.

1218
01:13:37.494 --> 01:13:38.997
[Dinwiddie]
Assassination.

1219
01:13:39.456 --> 01:13:42.880
You confessed to assassinating
a French Officer!

1220
01:13:43.380 --> 01:13:45.008
It was not my intention.
Your Excellency.

1221
01:13:45.133 --> 01:13:47.054
Is this not your signature?

1222
01:13:49.226 --> 01:13:51.313
Our intention had
never been to trouble peace.

1223
01:13:51.438 --> 01:13:52.816
but only to revenge

1224
01:13:52.941 --> 01:13:55.948
the assassination of
one of our officers.

1225
01:13:56.073 --> 01:13:57.157
The translator failed me. sir.

1226
01:13:57.284 --> 01:13:58.702
I didn't realize.
I thought that--

1227
01:13:58.827 --> 01:13:59.955
Washington.

1228
01:14:00.163 --> 01:14:03.420
To lead is to forfeit
the right to make excuses.

1229
01:14:04.214 --> 01:14:06.552
Have you any
idea what you've done?

1230
01:14:06.719 --> 01:14:08.681
You've started a war!
[slams desk]

1231
01:14:10.811 --> 01:14:12.229
I'll report that
the battle was lost

1232
01:14:12.355 --> 01:14:14.484
due to poor munitions
and lack of supplies.

1233
01:14:14.610 --> 01:14:16.822
But that is not the truth. sir.

1234
01:14:17.030 --> 01:14:19.537
That is the truth
that suits me. otherwise--

1235
01:14:19.662 --> 01:14:22.626
Sir. I came here
to resign my commission.

1236
01:14:25.966 --> 01:14:27.720
I am not fit to lead.

1237
01:14:28.804 --> 01:14:30.809
I was never fit to lead.

1238
01:14:35.233 --> 01:14:36.529
God save the King.

1239
01:14:40.243 --> 01:14:43.792
And your resignation would
say that I'm not fit to choose.

1240
01:14:43.917 --> 01:14:46.131
Washington. you
abandon this office.

1241
01:14:46.256 --> 01:14:49.096
you abandon your
ambition with it.

1242
01:14:49.597 --> 01:14:50.724
Understood. sir.

1243
01:15:24.875 --> 01:15:26.294
Where's Lawrence?

1244
01:15:31.847 --> 01:15:33.350
I'm sorry.

1245
01:15:55.143 --> 01:15:56.438
[screams]

1246
01:16:11.969 --> 01:16:14.474
He wanted you
to have his journals.

1247
01:16:17.773 --> 01:16:19.149
You were right.

1248
01:16:20.694 --> 01:16:22.489
You knew I would fail.

1249
01:16:23.659 --> 01:16:25.495
It's not your fault. George.

1250
01:16:25.621 --> 01:16:29.044
You did not lay your
brother low. Nor those men.

1251
01:16:31.299 --> 01:16:32.678
I chose the ground.

1252
01:16:33.220 --> 01:16:35.223
I put on the coat.
I gave the order.

1253
01:16:35.348 --> 01:16:37.227
And now
because of that...

1254
01:16:39.858 --> 01:16:41.361
Good men are dead.

1255
01:16:50.337 --> 01:16:52.174
When your father died.

1256
01:16:53.135 --> 01:16:57.184
there were accounts
I could not read.

1257
01:16:58.061 --> 01:17:02.905
acres I could not plow.
But I learned. as women do.

1258
01:17:03.822 --> 01:17:08.624
to keep a tally with one hand
and a prayer with the other.

1259
01:17:08.749 --> 01:17:14.092
I hardened because
the wind here is hard.

1260
01:17:14.803 --> 01:17:17.224
Put iron in my voice.

1261
01:17:18.686 --> 01:17:20.606
I was hard on you. George.

1262
01:17:21.900 --> 01:17:26.326
I see you learned
to be hard on yourself.

1263
01:17:27.202 --> 01:17:28.539
That was my sin.

1264
01:17:38.684 --> 01:17:41.189
You said Providence
placed me here.

1265
01:17:45.948 --> 01:17:46.867
Why?

1266
01:17:48.662 --> 01:17:50.207
For me to fail?

1267
01:17:51.168 --> 01:17:52.002
Perhaps.

1268
01:17:54.424 --> 01:17:56.804
Failure is
the tutor sent by God.

1269
01:17:57.848 --> 01:18:00.143
If you don't learn from it.
you've failed twice.

1270
01:18:00.268 --> 01:18:03.734
If you do learn from it.
you've earned wisdom.

1271
01:18:05.445 --> 01:18:06.239
So...

1272
01:18:07.826 --> 01:18:09.327
What did it tell you?

1273
01:18:11.667 --> 01:18:12.710
To go back.

1274
01:18:16.885 --> 01:18:18.305
But I'm afraid...

1275
01:18:19.389 --> 01:18:20.851
of making the same mistakes.

1276
01:18:25.485 --> 01:18:30.412
War is not the path I would
choose for you. But...

1277
01:18:31.373 --> 01:18:32.249
Oh...

1278
01:18:32.708 --> 01:18:34.713
On your feet. son.

1279
01:18:38.261 --> 01:18:43.814
If you must
return to soldiering. go.

1280
01:18:46.695 --> 01:18:50.828
As God's servant.
Do it with your whole heart.

1281
01:18:52.455 --> 01:18:53.709
Find your path.

1282
01:18:54.670 --> 01:18:55.671
Make it yours.

1283
01:18:56.256 --> 01:18:57.465
Make it straight.

1284
01:19:00.263 --> 01:19:01.850
And prove them wrong.

1285
01:19:06.985 --> 01:19:10.283
Because even a
pawn can take the king.

1286
01:19:23.393 --> 01:19:26.106
[dramatic music]

1287
01:19:48.611 --> 01:19:50.405
[drum beat plays]

1288
01:20:12.866 --> 01:20:14.452
I'm sorry to disturb. sir.

1289
01:20:15.205 --> 01:20:16.625
I am George Washington.

1290
01:20:16.750 --> 01:20:17.417
Ah!

1291
01:20:18.837 --> 01:20:20.549
The reason I am here.

1292
01:20:21.802 --> 01:20:23.639
Meet Colonel Thomas Gage.

1293
01:20:24.892 --> 01:20:26.979
Gage has recently
been promoted to colonel

1294
01:20:27.104 --> 01:20:28.524
by Royal Commission.

1295
01:20:28.982 --> 01:20:29.943
We’ve met.

1296
01:20:30.235 --> 01:20:33.366
I'm assuming you
seek your previous command.

1297
01:20:33.491 --> 01:20:35.829
Gage has been tasked
with leading your militia

1298
01:20:35.954 --> 01:20:38.126
and is far more qualified.

1299
01:20:38.627 --> 01:20:39.838
I'm sure he is.

1300
01:20:40.130 --> 01:20:42.175
I neither ask for rank nor pay.

1301
01:20:42.300 --> 01:20:44.304
I'm here to volunteer
as your aide-de-camp.

1302
01:20:44.429 --> 01:20:45.891
I believe I could be
of some assistance to you.

1303
01:20:46.016 --> 01:20:47.394
Oh. do not worry.

1304
01:20:47.645 --> 01:20:50.818
Young Washington. These uh.
these French and their savages

1305
01:20:50.943 --> 01:20:54.407
may have been a formidable enemy
to you and your militia.

1306
01:20:54.533 --> 01:20:58.667
but to the King's troops. they
are more of a nuisance. really.

1307
01:20:58.792 --> 01:21:00.879
Bit of a waste of powder.

1308
01:21:01.213 --> 01:21:03.552
We will prevail. With ease.

1309
01:21:03.677 --> 01:21:04.763
But with all due respect. sir.

1310
01:21:04.888 --> 01:21:07.017
I do not think
it will be with ease.

1311
01:21:07.142 --> 01:21:09.062
-Having fought--
-And lost.

1312
01:21:09.271 --> 01:21:11.066
Having fought
within the region. sir.

1313
01:21:11.191 --> 01:21:12.903
I believe I could
be of some help to you.

1314
01:21:13.028 --> 01:21:14.489
Fort Duquesne is difficult.

1315
01:21:14.615 --> 01:21:18.582
Duquesne can hardly detain me
above three or four days.

1316
01:21:18.707 --> 01:21:21.169
Sir. this is a very
different type of battle.

1317
01:21:21.294 --> 01:21:23.216
Just the trip to the fort
alone is treach--

1318
01:21:23.341 --> 01:21:24.384
A week at most.

1319
01:21:24.510 --> 01:21:25.220
A month.

1320
01:21:26.138 --> 01:21:26.932
A month?

1321
01:21:27.182 --> 01:21:28.100
If lucky.

1322
01:21:29.394 --> 01:21:30.105
For most of the journey.

1323
01:21:30.230 --> 01:21:31.356
you'll be
traveling a single file.

1324
01:21:31.483 --> 01:21:33.278
over what is barely a trail.

1325
01:21:33.403 --> 01:21:35.323
Not even wide enough for wagons.

1326
01:21:35.448 --> 01:21:36.408
I've surveyed the land.

1327
01:21:36.535 --> 01:21:37.745
I know this land.

1328
01:21:38.246 --> 01:21:40.584
The French are located here.
where the three rivers meet.

1329
01:21:40.709 --> 01:21:43.005
Because of the land. the style
of warfare is. uh.

1330
01:21:43.130 --> 01:21:44.592
it's different.

1331
01:21:44.968 --> 01:21:46.219
These are not the
open battlefields

1332
01:21:46.344 --> 01:21:47.222
to which you're accustomed.

1333
01:21:47.347 --> 01:21:50.312
I have fought on
a great many battlefields.

1334
01:21:50.437 --> 01:21:51.774
Not in the new world. sir.

1335
01:21:51.899 --> 01:21:53.902
You lost in the new world.

1336
01:21:57.868 --> 01:21:59.162
Yes.

1337
01:21:59.329 --> 01:22:00.457
You're right.

1338
01:22:00.749 --> 01:22:02.961
But failure is a great teacher.

1339
01:22:05.383 --> 01:22:06.762
I desire to serve under
someone of your ability

1340
01:22:06.887 --> 01:22:08.974
and experience to learn more.

1341
01:22:09.474 --> 01:22:10.268
Sir.

1342
01:22:15.946 --> 01:22:19.327
You may come. As advisor
and aide. That is all.

1343
01:22:20.455 --> 01:22:21.834
Thank you. General Braddock.

1344
01:22:21.959 --> 01:22:24.588
Colonel Gage see
that he is accommodated.

1345
01:22:24.713 --> 01:22:25.799
Yes. sir.

1346
01:22:29.557 --> 01:22:31.854
[drum beat plays]

1347
01:23:01.789 --> 01:23:03.081
[Braddock] What is the delay?

1348
01:23:03.290 --> 01:23:04.334
Move these wagons.

1349
01:23:04.459 --> 01:23:05.796
So. Washington.

1350
01:23:07.132 --> 01:23:11.223
From colonel to aide-de-camp.
How the mighty have fallen.

1351
01:23:11.431 --> 01:23:14.437
Well. I was never given
the Royal Commission as colonel.

1352
01:23:14.563 --> 01:23:16.191
so did it truly matter?

1353
01:23:17.778 --> 01:23:19.281
This is important to you?

1354
01:23:19.406 --> 01:23:20.576
Fairness? Yes.

1355
01:23:21.619 --> 01:23:24.917
Gage. what on
God's earth is the delay here?

1356
01:23:25.293 --> 01:23:26.461
Fallen tree. I believe. sir.

1357
01:23:26.587 --> 01:23:27.881
Well. how-how do you expect
to win a battle

1358
01:23:28.006 --> 01:23:29.510
if you can't
even defeat a tree?

1359
01:23:29.635 --> 01:23:30.303
Yes. sir.

1360
01:23:30.804 --> 01:23:34.728
I have fought the King's battles
on three continents.

1361
01:23:34.978 --> 01:23:37.901
but never have I
been defeated by a tree.

1362
01:23:38.821 --> 01:23:40.616
[Braddock] This is no army.

1363
01:23:40.824 --> 01:23:43.203
This is a centipede with gout.

1364
01:23:45.417 --> 01:23:48.171
[Tucker] Henry. David.
Look who's here.

1365
01:23:51.094 --> 01:23:52.055
Major?

1366
01:23:52.305 --> 01:23:53.934
Aide-de-camp.

1367
01:23:54.727 --> 01:23:57.274
It seems you're my
superiors. actually.

1368
01:23:58.358 --> 01:24:00.823
Take up an axe
and help us with this tree.

1369
01:24:01.323 --> 01:24:02.200
Gladly.

1370
01:24:09.507 --> 01:24:11.343
[Gage] What seems to
be the delay?

1371
01:24:11.468 --> 01:24:12.971
I'm sorry. Colonel.

1372
01:24:13.473 --> 01:24:14.975
There's no damn road.

1373
01:24:16.019 --> 01:24:17.230
That's the delay.

1374
01:24:18.692 --> 01:24:20.821
[Gage] Washington.
these are your friends?

1375
01:24:21.363 --> 01:24:23.200
Why do they not wear
the King’s red?

1376
01:24:23.325 --> 01:24:24.161
Or at least try?

1377
01:24:24.286 --> 01:24:26.414
You stole our last uniforms.

1378
01:24:26.959 --> 01:24:28.796
Thievin' bastards.

1379
01:24:29.296 --> 01:24:32.385
See. uh. indigo
grows wild around here.

1380
01:24:32.886 --> 01:24:34.222
We use it for blue dye.

1381
01:24:34.347 --> 01:24:35.559
That's the color of Virginia.

1382
01:24:35.684 --> 01:24:36.895
You boys go’head.

1383
01:24:37.020 --> 01:24:40.067
wear all them pretty colors
and get shot first.

1384
01:24:40.193 --> 01:24:43.406
I’ll blend into the woods
and die an ol’ man.

1385
01:24:49.545 --> 01:24:52.175
What happened
with your grand design?

1386
01:24:53.218 --> 01:24:54.680
Royal commission.

1387
01:24:55.849 --> 01:24:57.060
Little rich girl.

1388
01:24:57.603 --> 01:25:00.984
I buried those plans
when I buried Christopher.

1389
01:25:08.373 --> 01:25:09.793
Why'd you come back?

1390
01:25:10.420 --> 01:25:12.424
Came back to apologize.

1391
01:25:13.636 --> 01:25:15.347
My ambition was selfish.

1392
01:25:15.848 --> 01:25:18.519
I owe a debt to
every single one of you.

1393
01:25:18.646 --> 01:25:20.733
A debt I cannot repay. but...

1394
01:25:22.069 --> 01:25:26.619
When the time comes
for battle. I will be there.

1395
01:25:27.079 --> 01:25:29.041
Fighting beside you.

1396
01:25:32.130 --> 01:25:33.215
Works for me.

1397
01:25:35.679 --> 01:25:36.847
[Henry chuckles]

1398
01:25:46.534 --> 01:25:47.870
[low rumbling sound]

1399
01:25:47.995 --> 01:25:49.247
[metal clinking]

1400
01:25:52.295 --> 01:25:54.800
[David] You need to place
a wager. George.

1401
01:25:58.431 --> 01:26:02.024
How about you. uh.
how about you place one for me?

1402
01:26:05.237 --> 01:26:07.242
You sure you're all right?

1403
01:26:08.619 --> 01:26:10.498
Yeah. never better.

1404
01:26:13.964 --> 01:26:16.218
-Thank you.
-Of course.

1405
01:26:20.561 --> 01:26:22.189
Excuse me.

1406
01:26:25.027 --> 01:26:26.572
Why are y'all here?

1407
01:26:27.240 --> 01:26:28.325
We were sent.

1408
01:26:28.534 --> 01:26:29.202
By who?

1409
01:26:29.537 --> 01:26:30.831
The Fairfaxes.

1410
01:26:30.998 --> 01:26:32.459
You'll fight for nobles?

1411
01:26:32.585 --> 01:26:34.337
We fight in their stead.

1412
01:26:41.935 --> 01:26:44.191
[piano plays softly]

1413
01:26:44.650 --> 01:26:46.028
Is that a piano?

1414
01:26:48.867 --> 01:26:49.952
Braddock's.

1415
01:26:50.621 --> 01:26:53.291
Hauled it all the way
from Alexandria.

1416
01:26:53.416 --> 01:26:54.377
I'm sorry.

1417
01:26:54.502 --> 01:26:58.176
We're cuttin' a road all the way
through the Ohio territory...

1418
01:26:58.301 --> 01:26:59.930
for a piano.

1419
01:27:04.773 --> 01:27:06.068
God help us.

1420
01:27:06.860 --> 01:27:09.241
[George] One. Two.
Three!

1421
01:27:09.366 --> 01:27:10.828
[men groan with effort]

1422
01:27:12.205 --> 01:27:13.373
-[David] Tucker!
-[Henry] Watch your feet.

1423
01:27:13.624 --> 01:27:14.668
[David] It's gettin'
stuck.

1424
01:27:14.793 --> 01:27:16.296
[overlapping chatter]

1425
01:27:16.755 --> 01:27:17.925
[David] Keep goin'!

1426
01:27:18.383 --> 01:27:19.427
[men groan with
effort]

1427
01:27:19.553 --> 01:27:20.514
[George groans in
pain]

1428
01:27:20.639 --> 01:27:21.599
[George coughs]

1429
01:27:21.724 --> 01:27:23.268
Hey. George.
You sure you're all right?

1430
01:27:24.522 --> 01:27:25.313
I'm fine.

1431
01:27:25.438 --> 01:27:26.483
Keep pushing. keep pushing.

1432
01:27:26.609 --> 01:27:27.444
We're nearly there.

1433
01:27:27.570 --> 01:27:29.698
[Braddock] You will acquaint
Mr. Hunter

1434
01:27:29.823 --> 01:27:32.454
that His Majesty’s service
requires the further sum

1435
01:27:32.580 --> 01:27:35.167
of 10.000 pounds sterling.

1436
01:27:36.294 --> 01:27:39.802
[Braddock] How else are we to
deal with the lack of roads

1437
01:27:40.052 --> 01:27:43.601
in a wilderness
that is proven formidable?

1438
01:27:44.269 --> 01:27:45.353
Did you get that?

1439
01:27:45.478 --> 01:27:46.607
Yes. Your Excellency.

1440
01:27:46.732 --> 01:27:48.110
Now. where was I?

1441
01:27:50.280 --> 01:27:52.745
The siege had been the
longest and the bloodiest...

1442
01:27:52.870 --> 01:27:53.662
[warbling voices]

1443
01:27:53.787 --> 01:27:54.582
Washington?

1444
01:27:54.707 --> 01:27:56.585
oh man. you’re pale as a ghost.

1445
01:27:59.675 --> 01:28:00.969
[Braddock muffled]
Washington.

1446
01:28:01.845 --> 01:28:02.973
[Braddock]
Washington!

1447
01:28:03.098 --> 01:28:03.976
Deliver the dispatch!

1448
01:28:04.101 --> 01:28:08.150
Sorry. Your Excellency. I was
lost in your story.

1449
01:28:16.458 --> 01:28:17.335
Gist!

1450
01:28:23.847 --> 01:28:24.975
[Gage] How is he?

1451
01:28:28.023 --> 01:28:29.359
Dysentery.

1452
01:28:29.735 --> 01:28:31.446
His case is very severe.

1453
01:28:32.072 --> 01:28:34.369
High fever.
terrible nightmares.

1454
01:28:34.494 --> 01:28:35.706
He calls out names.

1455
01:28:35.831 --> 01:28:37.710
How long will he be down?

1456
01:28:37.835 --> 01:28:42.050
Days. a week. forever.

1457
01:28:42.720 --> 01:28:43.971
Forever?

1458
01:28:44.181 --> 01:28:46.101
He'll survive. won't he?

1459
01:28:54.242 --> 01:28:55.243
Washington.

1460
01:28:58.876 --> 01:28:59.837
You're awake.

1461
01:29:00.420 --> 01:29:01.381
Where are we?

1462
01:29:01.799 --> 01:29:04.054
Five miles south of the river.
past the great meadows.

1463
01:29:04.179 --> 01:29:05.305
where you fought.

1464
01:29:05.430 --> 01:29:06.975
At Necessity. Yes.

1465
01:29:07.100 --> 01:29:11.109
I’ve been tasked with a command
of a flying column and 900 men.

1466
01:29:11.234 --> 01:29:13.071
We cross the
Monongahela River tomorrow.

1467
01:29:13.196 --> 01:29:15.786
The next day we
reach Fort Duquesne.

1468
01:29:16.119 --> 01:29:17.497
You should rest.

1469
01:29:17.665 --> 01:29:18.624
No!

1470
01:29:25.470 --> 01:29:26.765
Look to the trees.

1471
01:29:27.726 --> 01:29:30.648
This is a new world.
treat it that way.

1472
01:29:30.774 --> 01:29:32.528
Do you not think me
up to the task?

1473
01:29:32.653 --> 01:29:33.946
You weren't there.

1474
01:29:35.157 --> 01:29:36.952
I question the strategy.

1475
01:29:37.538 --> 01:29:38.664
[Nurse] That's enough.

1476
01:29:38.914 --> 01:29:40.794
Gage. look to the trees.

1477
01:29:42.129 --> 01:29:45.636
I've been preparing
for this all my life. George.

1478
01:29:50.395 --> 01:29:51.439
Courage. man.

1479
01:29:54.863 --> 01:29:56.241
God please help us.

1480
01:30:04.925 --> 01:30:07.387
[dramatic music]

1481
01:30:11.980 --> 01:30:13.358
Hold the advance.

1482
01:30:13.483 --> 01:30:15.195
[Soldier] Hold the
advance!

1483
01:30:15.487 --> 01:30:17.074
[Soldier] Hold the
advance.

1484
01:30:21.499 --> 01:30:23.336
[eerie music plays]

1485
01:30:25.382 --> 01:30:26.760
Advance the column.

1486
01:30:27.094 --> 01:30:28.597
[Soldier] Advance the
column.

1487
01:30:39.578 --> 01:30:41.832
[eerie music continues]

1488
01:30:48.721 --> 01:30:49.932
[bird call sound]

1489
01:30:50.307 --> 01:30:51.351
Halt!

1490
01:30:51.602 --> 01:30:52.688
[Soldier] Halt.

1491
01:30:56.779 --> 01:30:59.492
[man] Whoo!

1492
01:31:00.744 --> 01:31:03.000
[overlapping chatter]

1493
01:31:05.671 --> 01:31:06.715
[gunshot]

1494
01:31:08.218 --> 01:31:09.304
Ambush!

1495
01:31:09.555 --> 01:31:10.514
[men yelling]

1496
01:31:10.639 --> 01:31:11.600
[guns cock]

1497
01:31:11.725 --> 01:31:13.145
In line formation.

1498
01:31:14.898 --> 01:31:16.610
[Gage] In line
formation!

1499
01:31:19.324 --> 01:31:20.325
[men whooping]

1500
01:31:20.450 --> 01:31:21.328
Form square!

1501
01:31:21.662 --> 01:31:22.538
Form square!

1502
01:31:23.081 --> 01:31:25.502
Form square.
protect the column!

1503
01:31:26.421 --> 01:31:27.925
[gunshots impacting]

1504
01:31:28.759 --> 01:31:30.303
[men yelling and
whooping]

1505
01:31:39.321 --> 01:31:41.243
Number one section.
number two section.

1506
01:31:41.368 --> 01:31:42.661
In line formation.

1507
01:31:43.371 --> 01:31:46.712
Number one section.
present... fire.

1508
01:31:50.343 --> 01:31:53.726
Number two section.
present... fire.

1509
01:31:54.436 --> 01:31:56.857
Number one section.
number two section.

1510
01:31:56.982 --> 01:31:58.318
To my rear!

1511
01:31:58.902 --> 01:32:00.405
Protect the colors!

1512
01:32:01.158 --> 01:32:02.284
Get 'em to the river.

1513
01:32:02.492 --> 01:32:04.079
-[David] To the river!
-[Henry] To the river!

1514
01:32:04.204 --> 01:32:05.874
[inaudible yelling]

1515
01:32:06.251 --> 01:32:07.252
[Henry] To the river!

1516
01:32:07.377 --> 01:32:09.339
Get 'em to the river.
Come on!

1517
01:32:10.008 --> 01:32:11.554
We'll regroup at the river!

1518
01:32:11.679 --> 01:32:13.431
[cacophony of yelling
and gunfire]

1519
01:32:13.557 --> 01:32:14.602
Retreat!

1520
01:32:15.185 --> 01:32:16.313
[horse neighing]

1521
01:32:17.189 --> 01:32:19.109
[intense drum beats]

1522
01:32:23.661 --> 01:32:25.706
[Braddock] Make ready!
Present...

1523
01:32:26.625 --> 01:32:27.292
Fire!

1524
01:32:28.378 --> 01:32:30.257
[gunfire]

1525
01:32:30.382 --> 01:32:31.927
Build a rank. build a rank!

1526
01:32:32.052 --> 01:32:32.971
Build a line!

1527
01:32:33.430 --> 01:32:34.097
Move forward!

1528
01:32:34.222 --> 01:32:35.183
Move forward!

1529
01:32:36.353 --> 01:32:37.104
[gunfire]

1530
01:32:38.315 --> 01:32:39.777
Build a rank!

1531
01:32:40.110 --> 01:32:41.404
[Braddock] Hold the line!
Hold the line!

1532
01:32:42.239 --> 01:32:43.784
[intense. epic music]

1533
01:32:45.245 --> 01:32:46.749
[gunfire]

1534
01:32:48.669 --> 01:32:49.713
[cannon fire booms]

1535
01:32:59.022 --> 01:33:00.025
[cannon fire booms]

1536
01:33:02.696 --> 01:33:04.032
[gasping]

1537
01:33:10.253 --> 01:33:12.049
[cacophony of
gunfire and yelling]

1538
01:33:12.215 --> 01:33:13.594
[explosion]

1539
01:33:13.719 --> 01:33:14.888
What happened?

1540
01:33:15.472 --> 01:33:16.474
We've been ambushed!

1541
01:33:16.600 --> 01:33:17.434
From where?

1542
01:33:17.560 --> 01:33:18.562
Over the hill!

1543
01:33:19.732 --> 01:33:21.401
[gunfire]

1544
01:33:25.325 --> 01:33:28.791
[sounds muffle.
gasping as ringing starts]

1545
01:33:28.916 --> 01:33:30.252
[grunts with effort]

1546
01:33:34.342 --> 01:33:35.262
[gunfire]

1547
01:33:36.054 --> 01:33:37.725
[cannon fire]

1548
01:33:38.811 --> 01:33:40.856
[epic music]

1549
01:33:47.870 --> 01:33:49.247
I wouldn't bother.
Washington.

1550
01:33:49.833 --> 01:33:51.126
The battle's lost.

1551
01:33:52.212 --> 01:33:53.090
Where's the General?

1552
01:33:53.215 --> 01:33:54.718
Ordered a full retreat.

1553
01:33:54.843 --> 01:33:55.636
And my men?

1554
01:33:55.844 --> 01:33:56.764
You have no men.

1555
01:33:56.889 --> 01:33:57.975
The Virginians.

1556
01:33:58.892 --> 01:34:00.437
They were at the
front of the line.

1557
01:34:00.563 --> 01:34:02.525
It's nearly four
miles from here.

1558
01:34:03.193 --> 01:34:05.405
If you go that way.
you will die.

1559
01:34:06.281 --> 01:34:08.286
You look like death already.

1560
01:34:08.704 --> 01:34:09.915
Listen to me.

1561
01:34:11.919 --> 01:34:12.878
You'll never find them.

1562
01:34:13.005 --> 01:34:15.050
And even if you did.
you'd never make it back.

1563
01:34:15.718 --> 01:34:16.970
[bullet whizzes]

1564
01:34:17.095 --> 01:34:18.098
Washington.

1565
01:34:18.807 --> 01:34:19.768
Washington.

1566
01:34:20.644 --> 01:34:21.772
Come. my friend.

1567
01:34:22.815 --> 01:34:24.903
What could be worth the risk?

1568
01:34:28.243 --> 01:34:29.788
[dramatic stinger]

1569
01:34:29.913 --> 01:34:31.248
My men.

1570
01:34:36.258 --> 01:34:37.636
[epic music]

1571
01:34:42.605 --> 01:34:45.318
[explosions thunder]

1572
01:34:51.121 --> 01:34:52.124
[soldier grunts]

1573
01:34:57.092 --> 01:34:58.220
[cannon booms]

1574
01:34:59.429 --> 01:35:00.432
[groans]

1575
01:35:00.558 --> 01:35:01.852
[epic music continues]

1576
01:35:08.616 --> 01:35:09.952
[Indistinct yelling]

1577
01:35:10.285 --> 01:35:11.539
Where is the General?

1578
01:35:11.664 --> 01:35:12.956
Where is Braddock?

1579
01:35:13.081 --> 01:35:14.878
Hey! Listen to me!

1580
01:35:15.003 --> 01:35:16.464
-[bullet whizzes by]
-[horse neighs]

1581
01:35:16.882 --> 01:35:18.050
[groans]

1582
01:35:18.969 --> 01:35:21.431
Number one section.
Number two section.

1583
01:35:21.559 --> 01:35:22.851
Fix bayonets.

1584
01:35:24.479 --> 01:35:25.608
[cacophony of gunfire
and screams]

1585
01:35:25.733 --> 01:35:27.695
[yelling]

1586
01:35:27.903 --> 01:35:29.072
[indistinct yelling]

1587
01:35:30.576 --> 01:35:31.579
[groans]

1588
01:35:41.471 --> 01:35:43.393
[ominous tones]

1589
01:35:51.366 --> 01:35:52.953
[gunshots crack]

1590
01:35:55.333 --> 01:35:57.087
Where is the General?

1591
01:35:57.254 --> 01:35:58.674
[soldier] He's over
here!

1592
01:35:58.924 --> 01:35:59.968
Over here!

1593
01:36:02.931 --> 01:36:03.851
General.

1594
01:36:04.226 --> 01:36:04.895
General.

1595
01:36:05.228 --> 01:36:07.691
[panting]

1596
01:36:08.108 --> 01:36:09.194
Washington.

1597
01:36:09.737 --> 01:36:10.739
Sir.

1598
01:36:11.825 --> 01:36:12.910
You ordered a retreat?

1599
01:36:13.370 --> 01:36:15.874
I ordered no retreat.

1600
01:36:19.548 --> 01:36:22.137
Rally the men and fall back.

1601
01:36:24.432 --> 01:36:25.102
Wear...

1602
01:36:25.435 --> 01:36:26.144
Wear this.

1603
01:36:26.311 --> 01:36:28.023
They'll know it's mine.

1604
01:36:32.365 --> 01:36:37.960
Take my horse and save
as many as you can.

1605
01:36:40.674 --> 01:36:41.550
Yes. sir.

1606
01:36:43.305 --> 01:36:45.017
I won't let you down.

1607
01:36:46.729 --> 01:36:48.146
[dramatic music]

1608
01:36:50.443 --> 01:36:52.072
Who would have thought?

1609
01:36:53.867 --> 01:36:56.246
[inspiring music]

1610
01:36:58.586 --> 01:36:59.587
Retreat!

1611
01:36:59.712 --> 01:37:01.423
[booming thuds]

1612
01:37:03.470 --> 01:37:05.933
[George] Hold your ground.
there is no retreat.

1613
01:37:06.058 --> 01:37:07.185
This way!

1614
01:37:08.647 --> 01:37:10.067
There is no retreat.

1615
01:37:11.820 --> 01:37:13.616
Fall back! Fall back!

1616
01:37:13.741 --> 01:37:16.453
Hold your ground.
there is no retreat!

1617
01:37:16.662 --> 01:37:17.998
Hold fast!

1618
01:37:21.046 --> 01:37:22.174
Forward!

1619
01:37:24.553 --> 01:37:25.639
On me!

1620
01:37:26.264 --> 01:37:27.267
[Tucker] George!

1621
01:37:28.604 --> 01:37:29.855
Their advance ends here.

1622
01:37:29.980 --> 01:37:31.819
We will hold this line.

1623
01:37:32.110 --> 01:37:33.320
Fire and move!

1624
01:37:34.740 --> 01:37:36.076
Find cover in the trees.

1625
01:37:36.201 --> 01:37:37.580
Fire from the trees.

1626
01:37:37.705 --> 01:37:38.498
Spread out.

1627
01:37:38.666 --> 01:37:39.457
Spread out.

1628
01:37:40.335 --> 01:37:43.466
Men this is our land
and we will fight for it.

1629
01:37:43.592 --> 01:37:44.593
Independent fire.

1630
01:37:44.718 --> 01:37:45.638
Independent fire!

1631
01:37:47.474 --> 01:37:48.476
George!

1632
01:37:48.936 --> 01:37:49.603
Tucker.

1633
01:37:50.438 --> 01:37:51.356
Where are the others?

1634
01:37:51.481 --> 01:37:52.526
Where's David?
Where's Henry?

1635
01:37:52.651 --> 01:37:54.196
By the river. surrounded.

1636
01:37:54.321 --> 01:37:55.991
If they're still alive.

1637
01:37:56.116 --> 01:37:57.536
I'm going to try to reach them.

1638
01:37:57.661 --> 01:37:59.873
Tucker. rally as many as you can
and move to the river.

1639
01:37:59.998 --> 01:38:01.334
Wait for my signal.

1640
01:38:01.459 --> 01:38:02.921
I won't let you down. sir.

1641
01:38:03.046 --> 01:38:04.132
I'm no officer.

1642
01:38:04.299 --> 01:38:06.219
You are the only leader
on this field.

1643
01:38:06.344 --> 01:38:07.556
Buy me some time.

1644
01:38:09.768 --> 01:38:10.437
You there...

1645
01:38:10.563 --> 01:38:12.232
You. you. and you. follow
me. We'll get to the river.

1646
01:38:12.357 --> 01:38:13.316
On my command!

1647
01:38:13.441 --> 01:38:14.361
[groans]

1648
01:38:14.486 --> 01:38:15.531
Make ready.

1649
01:38:16.239 --> 01:38:17.242
[horse neighs]

1650
01:38:17.367 --> 01:38:18.451
Fire!

1651
01:38:18.829 --> 01:38:20.541
[gunshots ring out]

1652
01:38:23.672 --> 01:38:26.051
[loud booming thuds]

1653
01:38:27.805 --> 01:38:29.307
[men yelling]

1654
01:38:30.686 --> 01:38:31.562
[gunshot]

1655
01:38:32.606 --> 01:38:34.985
Argh! You damn British guns.

1656
01:38:36.530 --> 01:38:37.533
[Sam whimpers]

1657
01:38:37.658 --> 01:38:39.537
No. No. No. Sam.
stay with me. son.

1658
01:38:39.662 --> 01:38:41.875
Brits left us here to die.

1659
01:38:42.125 --> 01:38:43.629
You sound surprised.

1660
01:38:44.296 --> 01:38:45.298
[Charles] Sam...

1661
01:38:48.806 --> 01:38:50.015
[Henry] How many
rounds left?

1662
01:38:50.182 --> 01:38:52.479
My gun doesn't even work. Henry.

1663
01:38:53.313 --> 01:38:54.525
[gunshots ringing]

1664
01:38:55.611 --> 01:38:56.820
Check for powder.

1665
01:39:00.453 --> 01:39:01.329
[horse neighs]

1666
01:39:02.165 --> 01:39:03.333
Henry. look.

1667
01:39:04.336 --> 01:39:05.589
[Henry] Is that...

1668
01:39:05.881 --> 01:39:07.551
[epic music]

1669
01:39:10.891 --> 01:39:12.185
It's Washington.

1670
01:39:12.310 --> 01:39:13.606
Man's a damn fool.

1671
01:39:17.863 --> 01:39:18.782
[grunts]

1672
01:39:18.907 --> 01:39:20.828
Come on.

1673
01:39:20.953 --> 01:39:22.122
[gunshots]

1674
01:39:22.247 --> 01:39:23.498
[grunting]

1675
01:39:28.592 --> 01:39:29.970
[yelling]

1676
01:39:30.639 --> 01:39:31.890
[gunshot]

1677
01:39:43.496 --> 01:39:44.542
-They're behind us.
-[David] Huh?

1678
01:39:44.792 --> 01:39:46.461
They flanked you
from the right side.

1679
01:39:46.587 --> 01:39:47.715
Well. what do we do?

1680
01:39:47.840 --> 01:39:48.507
We fight.

1681
01:39:48.632 --> 01:39:50.218
We're all out of power.

1682
01:39:51.555 --> 01:39:53.183
Has anybody got powder?

1683
01:39:53.391 --> 01:39:54.061
Who has powder?

1684
01:39:54.186 --> 01:39:55.270
Here! I got it!

1685
01:39:57.693 --> 01:39:58.821
Let's make 'em pay.

1686
01:40:00.113 --> 01:40:01.742
Reload every weapon
you can find.

1687
01:40:01.867 --> 01:40:03.997
Men of Virginia.
reload your weapons.

1688
01:40:04.122 --> 01:40:05.709
To the right. follow me.

1689
01:40:05.834 --> 01:40:08.171
Keep that powder on you
and keep it dry.

1690
01:40:08.380 --> 01:40:10.385
Let's go. let's go!
Let's give'em hell.

1691
01:40:11.428 --> 01:40:12.765
[David] Keep your
head down. Henry.

1692
01:40:13.015 --> 01:40:13.976
[grunting]

1693
01:40:14.101 --> 01:40:16.354
[George] Virginians. take
cover along the berm!

1694
01:40:18.483 --> 01:40:20.362
Keep your heads down.

1695
01:40:20.823 --> 01:40:22.660
[cacophony of gunfire
and cannon explosions]

1696
01:40:27.961 --> 01:40:30.132
Reload your muskets.

1697
01:40:32.555 --> 01:40:34.767
Ahh... you bastard.

1698
01:40:35.435 --> 01:40:36.520
Make ready.

1699
01:40:37.856 --> 01:40:38.942
Ready?

1700
01:40:39.067 --> 01:40:40.152
Present arms!

1701
01:40:42.533 --> 01:40:43.576
Fire!

1702
01:40:45.328 --> 01:40:46.206
Second rank.

1703
01:40:49.880 --> 01:40:50.674
Make ready.

1704
01:40:51.509 --> 01:40:52.427
Present arms.

1705
01:40:53.303 --> 01:40:54.306
Fire!

1706
01:40:58.271 --> 01:41:01.444
On my signal. take the men
as fast as you can to the right.

1707
01:41:01.570 --> 01:41:03.365
What are you going to do?

1708
01:41:06.246 --> 01:41:07.625
George.

1709
01:41:08.250 --> 01:41:09.670
[epic music]

1710
01:41:14.179 --> 01:41:15.430
[gunfire]

1711
01:41:22.613 --> 01:41:24.491
He's makin’ himself a target.

1712
01:41:26.787 --> 01:41:28.582
[epic music]

1713
01:41:31.880 --> 01:41:33.258
[speaking Seneca]

1714
01:41:37.851 --> 01:41:39.229
[bullets whizzing]

1715
01:41:48.831 --> 01:41:49.750
Now!

1716
01:41:50.042 --> 01:41:50.878
Now!

1717
01:41:53.048 --> 01:41:54.051
[Tucker] Present!

1718
01:41:55.343 --> 01:41:56.304
Fire!

1719
01:41:58.517 --> 01:41:59.477
[Tucker] Freedom!

1720
01:41:59.603 --> 01:42:01.231
Independent fire!

1721
01:42:01.857 --> 01:42:04.362
[muskets cracking]

1722
01:42:04.655 --> 01:42:06.992
Men of Virginia. to the right!

1723
01:42:07.911 --> 01:42:09.289
[George] Go! Go!

1724
01:42:09.873 --> 01:42:11.376
[triumphant music]

1725
01:42:14.299 --> 01:42:15.928
[explosions thunder]

1726
01:42:24.570 --> 01:42:26.782
[dramatic music
intensifies]

1727
01:42:45.443 --> 01:42:47.114
[distant gunshots]

1728
01:42:54.588 --> 01:42:58.011
Only tend to the ones who
you can see breathing.

1729
01:42:58.136 --> 01:42:59.056
What is that?

1730
01:43:01.977 --> 01:43:04.942
[triumphant music]

1731
01:43:06.820 --> 01:43:08.115
[birds chirping]

1732
01:43:31.995 --> 01:43:34.126
[triumphant music continues]

1733
01:43:54.207 --> 01:43:55.751
What's wrong. sir?

1734
01:43:56.754 --> 01:43:57.965
Seen a ghost?

1735
01:43:58.549 --> 01:44:00.260
[triumphant music]

1736
01:44:10.322 --> 01:44:11.158
There was no order.

1737
01:44:11.283 --> 01:44:11.950
What?

1738
01:44:12.200 --> 01:44:13.286
To retreat.

1739
01:44:18.964 --> 01:44:21.053
The battle was lost. George.

1740
01:44:22.012 --> 01:44:25.102
I see no point in
joining him in the grave.

1741
01:44:26.104 --> 01:44:28.275
Whose land is this. anyway?

1742
01:44:29.236 --> 01:44:30.445
It's our land.

1743
01:44:30.906 --> 01:44:33.160
Well. my land is an ocean away.

1744
01:44:40.799 --> 01:44:43.806
See. that is the
difference between us.

1745
01:44:51.947 --> 01:44:53.075
You all right?

1746
01:44:53.241 --> 01:44:54.620
How are the others?

1747
01:44:55.037 --> 01:44:56.206
We lost a lot of men.

1748
01:44:56.331 --> 01:44:57.332
How many?

1749
01:44:58.460 --> 01:44:59.630
Hundreds.

1750
01:45:01.091 --> 01:45:02.928
[solemn music]

1751
01:45:10.693 --> 01:45:15.452
Thank you for
coming back for us.

1752
01:45:21.507 --> 01:45:25.013
Major Washington. the Half-King.

1753
01:45:31.068 --> 01:45:33.196
[ominous music]

1754
01:45:49.647 --> 01:45:51.274
So. now you fight
for the French?

1755
01:45:51.984 --> 01:45:54.907
I no longer fight wars
that are not my own.

1756
01:45:55.032 --> 01:45:56.619
Then why are you here?

1757
01:45:57.119 --> 01:45:57.996
To find you.

1758
01:45:59.875 --> 01:46:00.876
Follow me.

1759
01:46:02.756 --> 01:46:04.132
[ominous music
builds]

1760
01:46:10.813 --> 01:46:12.232
[speaking Native language]

1761
01:46:13.110 --> 01:46:15.531
He wants to know who you are.

1762
01:46:17.242 --> 01:46:18.203
Why?

1763
01:46:20.248 --> 01:46:21.877
[speaking Native language]

1764
01:46:27.429 --> 01:46:30.268
I ordered my
warriors to shoot you.

1765
01:46:30.728 --> 01:46:31.980
All of them.

1766
01:46:33.609 --> 01:46:35.112
My men never miss.

1767
01:46:36.239 --> 01:46:39.036
[speaking Native language]

1768
01:46:47.595 --> 01:46:50.934
Our people have a legend.

1769
01:46:51.729 --> 01:46:54.818
A spirit of protection that
shields those chosen.

1770
01:46:54.943 --> 01:46:56.822
those who walk in destiny.

1771
01:46:56.989 --> 01:47:00.495
[speaking Native language]

1772
01:47:00.996 --> 01:47:02.457
Creator chose you.

1773
01:47:02.918 --> 01:47:05.088
You've been
shielded by the spirit.

1774
01:47:05.213 --> 01:47:08.261
[speaking Native language]

1775
01:47:08.386 --> 01:47:09.513
So. I ask again.

1776
01:47:09.765 --> 01:47:11.183
What are you called?

1777
01:47:14.314 --> 01:47:16.403
My name is George Washington.

1778
01:47:18.532 --> 01:47:19.993
[speaking Native language]

1779
01:47:22.831 --> 01:47:24.712
I will remember this name.

1780
01:47:28.426 --> 01:47:30.723
[Dinwiddie] Are those bullet
holes in your jacket?

1781
01:47:31.014 --> 01:47:31.725
Apologies.

1782
01:47:31.892 --> 01:47:33.145
sir. this is
the only uniform I own--

1783
01:47:33.270 --> 01:47:34.982
You misunderstand my statement.

1784
01:47:35.107 --> 01:47:36.024
And your hat?

1785
01:47:36.652 --> 01:47:38.656
Yes. it's the
only one I own as well.

1786
01:47:38.781 --> 01:47:39.825
The militia is in general--

1787
01:47:39.950 --> 01:47:42.538
It also has a
bullet hole in it.

1788
01:47:45.669 --> 01:47:47.255
How are you alive?

1789
01:47:48.842 --> 01:47:50.679
A divine hand. perhaps.

1790
01:47:50.888 --> 01:47:51.807
Perhaps.

1791
01:47:52.224 --> 01:47:53.351
That says maybe.

1792
01:47:54.311 --> 01:47:57.067
But you are
the man of the hour.

1793
01:47:57.317 --> 01:47:58.403
That's certain.

1794
01:47:58.696 --> 01:48:00.783
Your journals to the council.
they've been published

1795
01:48:00.908 --> 01:48:02.077
and have made
you quite well known.

1796
01:48:02.202 --> 01:48:03.831
They've even awakened London

1797
01:48:03.956 --> 01:48:06.001
to the situation our
colonies now face.

1798
01:48:06.126 --> 01:48:07.838
The way you
describe the frontier

1799
01:48:07.963 --> 01:48:11.261
has sparked the
imagination of many.

1800
01:48:13.058 --> 01:48:17.232
And. um... to your
recent actions.

1801
01:48:19.111 --> 01:48:22.117
Mr. Washington's
exemplary courage

1802
01:48:22.242 --> 01:48:25.666
was on full display as he evaded
many attacks on his person

1803
01:48:25.791 --> 01:48:29.214
while he felled
Indian and French enemies alike.

1804
01:48:29.339 --> 01:48:33.348
He also selflessly
rescued hundreds of his men

1805
01:48:33.473 --> 01:48:35.268
during a most
impressive retreat.

1806
01:48:35.393 --> 01:48:38.191
during which he continued
to battle the enemy with fervor.

1807
01:48:38.316 --> 01:48:40.153
despite his infirm condition.

1808
01:48:40.278 --> 01:48:41.907
Well. we were defeated.

1809
01:48:42.365 --> 01:48:45.163
Sir. 450 lives lost.
another 500 wounded.

1810
01:48:45.288 --> 01:48:46.289
But you have won.

1811
01:48:47.125 --> 01:48:48.754
Because you endured.

1812
01:48:49.840 --> 01:48:51.760
For most. failure is the end.

1813
01:48:51.885 --> 01:48:54.892
For you. it seems
only to be the beginning.

1814
01:48:55.017 --> 01:48:57.813
And since
leadership is the problem.

1815
01:49:00.277 --> 01:49:03.951
I'm going to give you
the opportunity to answer.

1816
01:49:04.284 --> 01:49:05.579
A second chance.

1817
01:49:07.666 --> 01:49:09.545
We're forming
a Virginia regiment.

1818
01:49:09.670 --> 01:49:11.842
1500 men. first of
its kind in the colonies.

1819
01:49:11.967 --> 01:49:13.303
and want you to lead it.

1820
01:49:13.428 --> 01:49:15.098
I'm reinstating your
rank as Colonel

1821
01:49:15.223 --> 01:49:16.602
in the Virginia Regiment.

1822
01:49:16.727 --> 01:49:18.606
And Commander
in Chief of all forces

1823
01:49:18.731 --> 01:49:21.737
raised in defense
of His Majesty's colony.

1824
01:49:22.320 --> 01:49:25.536
Do you accept
this great honor?

1825
01:49:28.375 --> 01:49:30.503
Yes. sir. I do.

1826
01:49:30.754 --> 01:49:31.674
Well then.

1827
01:49:32.090 --> 01:49:33.218
We have much to discuss.

1828
01:49:33.343 --> 01:49:35.514
I have...but one request.

1829
01:49:36.559 --> 01:49:40.023
Washington. if you ask for equal
pay or a royal commission--

1830
01:49:40.148 --> 01:49:40.983
No. sir.

1831
01:49:42.319 --> 01:49:44.908
I would like to
discuss the uniform.

1832
01:49:50.002 --> 01:49:51.003
Fall in!

1833
01:50:14.842 --> 01:50:17.055
Form up on Colonel Washington!

1834
01:50:21.774 --> 01:50:23.694
I am not a British officer.

1835
01:50:26.700 --> 01:50:29.162
I am not a
gentleman of England.

1836
01:50:31.041 --> 01:50:34.548
I have no title.
no royal commission.

1837
01:50:37.220 --> 01:50:39.349
But what I do have is you.

1838
01:50:41.394 --> 01:50:42.480
All of you.

1839
01:50:45.278 --> 01:50:46.740
I am a Virginian.

1840
01:50:49.662 --> 01:50:52.250
And it is my
honor to serve you.

1841
01:50:53.210 --> 01:50:54.672
To Virginia!

1842
01:50:54.880 --> 01:50:56.216
[men] To Virginia!

1843
01:50:56.424 --> 01:50:58.178
[men yell and cheer]

1844
01:51:09.326 --> 01:51:10.746
To Virginia.

1845
01:51:19.096 --> 01:51:20.808
[dramatic music]

1846
01:52:02.015 --> 01:52:04.728
[dramatic music]

1847
01:52:29.486 --> 01:52:30.698
Thank you
for being here tonight.

1848
01:52:31.031 --> 01:52:32.242
You're not
just watching a film.

1849
01:52:32.618 --> 01:52:33.829
you're helping launch a movement

1850
01:52:34.454 --> 01:52:36.291
because the ideals
at the heart of this country

1851
01:52:36.792 --> 01:52:37.502
still matter.

1852
01:52:37.795 --> 01:52:39.464
We believe the story
of George Washington.

1853
01:52:40.132 --> 01:52:43.557
of sacrifice. courage.
humility. perseverance.

1854
01:52:43.682 --> 01:52:45.227
and faith still matters.

1855
01:52:46.019 --> 01:52:48.356
Freedom matters.
virtue matters.

1856
01:52:48.817 --> 01:52:51.154
The belief that
liberty is worth fighting for.

1857
01:52:52.365 --> 01:52:53.366
that still matters.

1858
01:52:53.911 --> 01:52:56.373
So we are inviting
you tonight to Pay it Forward

1859
01:52:56.540 --> 01:52:58.587
because when you do.
you give countless families

1860
01:52:58.712 --> 01:53:00.005
the chance to see
Young Washington.

1861
01:53:00.298 --> 01:53:02.177
and with your help.
Young Washington

1862
01:53:02.385 --> 01:53:04.682
can be America's
number one movie.

